7:content;268891:{"max_tokens":32768,"messages":[{"content":[{"text":"---\n## ‚ö° Entering Phase: Execute\nYou are now in the **Execute** phase. Set aside any planning considerations or review feedback from previous phases ‚Äî they no longer apply. Your only objective is defined below.\n---\n\nImplement the plan below precisely, file by file.\n\nThe Explore and Plan phases are complete. File contents read during those phases are available in the conversation history ‚Äî check there before calling `read_file` to avoid reading the same file twice. If the content you need is not in the history, read it from disk using `read_file`.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Follow the plan exactly ‚Äî do not add features, refactor unrelated code, or make unrequested improvements\n- Check conversation history for file content before calling `read_file`\n- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones\n- Do not add comments, docstrings, or type annotations to code you did not change\n- If you hit an unexpected blocker, stop and ask rather than working around it\n\n\u003cplan\u003e\n## Refactoring Plan for export_flows.py\n\n### Analysis of Current State\n\nThe file `/workspace/export_flows.py` is a single 600+ line module containing several distinct functional areas:\n\n1. **Constants and pricing data** - `MODEL_PRICING`, `SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX`, `_SORTED_PREFIXES`, `AGENT_COLORS`, `READ_TOOLS`, `WRITE_TOOLS`, `_PROJECT_ROOT`, `_REDACTED_HEADERS`\n2. **Model utilities** - `get_canonical_model()`, `get_pricing()`\n3. **Path/string utilities** - `sanitize_path()`, `count_whitespace_stats()`, `_resolve_read_file_name()`, `_format_tool_params()`\n4. **Flow I/O** - `format_headers()`, `write_request()`, `write_response()`, `redact_flow_files()`, `export_flows()`\n5. **Response parsing** - `extract_stop_reason()`, `parse_response_content()`, `export_parsed_response()`, `export_parsed_responses()`, `categorize_output_sources()`\n6. **Request analysis** - `parse_request_body()`, `_get_file_path()`, `extract_read_file_whitespace()`, `categorize_input_sources()`, `_system_prompt_hash()`\n7. **Usage/cost processing** - `extract_usage()`, `calculate_costs()`, `extract_source_attribution()`, `attribute_tokens()`, `extract_file_ops()`\n8. **Summary/aggregation** - `summarize_usage()`, `_aggregate_by_source()`, `_round_by_source()`, `_finalize_file_ops()` (nested), `_finalize_timing()` (nested), `_agent_color()`\n9. **CLI entry point** - `main()`\n\nThe test file `/workspace/test_export_flows.py` imports everything as `import export_flows as ef`, meaning all public names must remain accessible via that module.\n\n### Design Decision: Modular Split with Re-exports\n\nThe safest approach that preserves all external behavior is:\n\n1. Split into sub-modules under a package, OR\n2. Split into sibling modules and import everything back into `export_flows.py`\n\n**Chosen approach: Sibling modules with re-exports in export_flows.py**\n\nThis is the safest strategy because:\n- The test file does `import export_flows as ef` and calls `ef.function_name()`\n- All public names must remain accessible as `ef.function_name`\n- A flat namespace re-export in `export_flows.py` preserves this without changing any test code\n- Each new module is independently testable\n- Refactoring is incremental ‚Äî one module at a time, tests run after each step\n\n### Module Split Plan\n\nThe file will be split into 4 new modules (numbered for implementation order):\n\n**Step 1: Extract `models.py`**\n- Constants: `MODEL_PRICING`, `SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX`, `_SORTED_PREFIXES`, `AGENT_COLORS`\n- Functions: `get_canonical_model()`, `get_pricing()`, `_agent_color()`\n- No dependencies on other new modules\n- Re-export in `export_flows.py` via `from models import *` (or explicit names)\n\n**Step 2: Extract `parsing.py`**\n- Constants: `_REDACTED_HEADERS`, `READ_TOOLS`, `WRITE_TOOLS`, `_PROJECT_ROOT`\n- Functions: `sanitize_path()`, `count_whitespace_stats()`, `_resolve_read_file_name()`, `_format_tool_params()`, `format_headers()`, `_get_file_path()`, `parse_request_body()`, `extract_stop_reason()`, `_system_prompt_hash()`\n- Depends on: nothing from other new modules\n- Re-export in `export_flows.py`\n\n**Step 3: Extract `response.py`**\n- Functions: `parse_response_content()`, `export_parsed_response()`, `export_parsed_responses()`, `categorize_output_sources()`\n- Depends on: `parsing.py` (for `_resolve_read_file_name`, `_format_tool_params`)\n- Re-export in `export_flows.py`\n\n**Step 4: Extract `usage.py`**\n- Functions: `extract_usage()`, `calculate_costs()`, `extract_source_attribution()`, `attribute_tokens()`, `extract_file_ops()`, `extract_read_file_whitespace()`, `categorize_input_sources()`, `_aggregate_by_source()`, `_round_by_source()`, `summarize_usage()`\n- Depends on: `models.py` (for `get_pricing`, `get_canonical_model`, `AGENT_COLORS`, `_agent_color`), `parsing.py` (for `parse_request_body`, `_resolve_read_file_name`, `_get_file_path`, `_system_prompt_hash`), `response.py` (for `parse_response_content`, `categorize_output_sources`)\n- Re-export in `export_flows.py`\n\n**Step 5: Slim down `export_flows.py`**\n- Keeps: `write_request()`, `write_response()`, `redact_flow_files()`, `export_flows()`, `main()`\n- Adds: import re-exports from all 4 new modules so `ef.X` still works for every public name\n- Depends on: all 4 new modules\n\n### Implementation Steps (with test runs)\n\n**Step 1**: Create `/workspace/models.py`\n- Move `MODEL_PRICING`, `SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX`, `_SORTED_PREFIXES`, `AGENT_COLORS`\n- Move `get_canonical_model()`, `get_pricing()`, `_agent_color()`\n- In `export_flows.py`: add `from models import MODEL_PRICING, SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX, AGENT_COLORS, get_canonical_model, get_pricing, _agent_color` at top, remove moved code\n- Run tests: `python -m pytest test_export_flows.py -v`\n\n**Step 2**: Create `/workspace/parsing.py`\n- Move `_REDACTED_HEADERS`, `READ_TOOLS`, `WRITE_TOOLS`, `_PROJECT_ROOT`\n- Move `sanitize_path()`, `count_whitespace_stats()`, `_resolve_read_file_name()`, `_format_tool_params()`, `format_headers()`, `_get_file_path()`, `parse_request_body()`, `extract_stop_reason()`, `_system_prompt_hash()`\n- `parsing.py` needs `from models import SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX` for `_system_prompt_hash`\n- In `export_flows.py`: add `from parsing import ...` for all moved names, remove moved code\n- Run tests\n\n**Step 3**: Create `/workspace/response.py`\n- Move `parse_response_content()`, `export_parsed_response()`, `export_parsed_responses()`, `categorize_output_sources()`\n- `response.py` needs `from parsing import _resolve_read_file_name, _format_tool_params`\n- In `export_flows.py`: add `from response import ...` for all moved names, remove moved code\n- Run tests\n\n**Step 4**: Create `/workspace/usage.py`\n- Move `extract_usage()`, `calculate_costs()`, `extract_source_attribution()`, `attribute_tokens()`, `extract_file_ops()`, `extract_read_file_whitespace()`, `categorize_input_sources()`, `_aggregate_by_source()`, `_round_by_source()`, `summarize_usage()`\n- `usage.py` needs imports from `models`, `parsing`, `response`\n- In `export_flows.py`: add `from usage import ...` for all moved names, remove moved code\n- Run tests\n\n**Step 5**: Clean up `export_flows.py`\n- Ensure all public names are re-exported explicitly (not via `*`) so that `ef.X` still works\n- Verify `main()` stays in `export_flows.py` and its pipeline calls still work\n- Run full test suite one final time\n\n### Key Constraints and Risks\n\n1. **Circular imports**: The dependency graph is strictly one-directional (`models` -\u003e `parsing` -\u003e `response` -\u003e `usage` -\u003e `export_flows`), so no circular imports will occur.\n\n2. **Private names with leading underscore**: The tests access `ef._resolve_read_file_name`, `ef._format_tool_params`, `ef._system_prompt_hash`, `ef._get_file_path`, `ef._agent_color`, `ef._aggregate_by_source`, `ef._round_by_source` directly. These must all be re-exported from `export_flows.py` by explicit name, even though they are \"private\" by convention.\n\n3. **Nested helper functions**: `summarize_usage()` contains nested functions `empty_bucket()`, `add_to_bucket()`, `round_costs()`, `_finalize_file_ops()`, `_finalize_timing()`. These are implementation details internal to `summarize_usage()` and should stay nested inside it in `usage.py`.\n\n4. **`_SORTED_PREFIXES`**: This is a module-level derived constant (`sorted(MODEL_PRICING.keys(), ...)`). It must be defined in `models.py` after `MODEL_PRICING` is defined.\n\n5. **`_PROJECT_ROOT`**: This uses `os.path.dirname(__file__)`. When moved to `parsing.py`, `__file__` will refer to `parsing.py`'s location ‚Äî which is the same directory `/workspace/`, so the value is identical.\n\n6. **The `export_flows` function name conflict**: The function `export_flows()` and the module `export_flows.py` share a name. The new sub-modules import from each other by name, not from `export_flows.py` directly, so there is no conflict.\n\n7. **Test for `export_flows()` function**: `TestExportFlows.test_exports_flows` asserts `\"Exported\"in output` but looking at the actual function body, it prints `f\"\\n{total} flows to {output_dir}\"` not \"Exported\". This test may already be failing or uses a string not present. This is pre-existing and must not be changed.\n\n### Re-export Strategy in export_flows.py\n\nThe explicit imports to add to `export_flows.py` (replacing moved code) will look like:\n\n```python\nfrom models import (\n    MODEL_PRICING, SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX, AGENT_COLORS,\n    get_canonical_model, get_pricing, _agent_color,\n)\nfrom parsing import (\n    _REDACTED_HEADERS, READ_TOOLS, WRITE_TOOLS,\n    sanitize_path, count_whitespace_stats, _resolve_read_file_name,\n    _format_tool_params, format_headers, _get_file_path,\n    parse_request_body, extract_stop_reason, _system_prompt_hash,\n)\nfrom response import (\n    parse_response_content, export_parsed_response,\n    export_parsed_responses, categorize_output_sources,\n)\nfrom usage import (\n    extract_usage, calculate_costs, extract_source_attribution,\n    attribute_tokens, extract_file_ops, extract_read_file_whitespace,\n    categorize_input_sources, _aggregate_by_source, _round_by_source,\n    summarize_usage,\n)\n```\n\nThis makes every `ef.X` call in the tests still work, since Python re-exports any name imported at module level.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `/workspace/export_flows.py` - Core file to refactor; keeps `write_request`, `write_response`, `redact_flow_files`, `export_flows`, `main`, plus re-exports\n- `/workspace/test_export_flows.py` - Test file to run after each step; must not be modified\n- `/workspace/models.py` - New module to create; first dependency layer (pricing, model lookup)\n- `/workspace/parsing.py` - New module to create; second dependency layer (string utils, header formatting, body parsing)\n- `/workspace/usage.py` - New module to create; top of dependency chain (cost calculation, aggregation)\n\u003c/plan\u003e","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"I'll implement the plan step by step, reading the current file first to ensure I have the latest content.","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_015ih8PM11gTfTkeb1MdS8ME","input":{"path":"/workspace/export_flows.py","reason":"Need to read the full current content before splitting into modules"},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ih8PM11gTfTkeb1MdS8ME","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"    1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n    2\t\"\"\"Export mitmproxy flow files into per-flow directories with request.json, request_headers.txt, and response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n    3\t\n    4\timport argparse\n    5\timport glob\n    6\timport hashlib\n    7\timport json\n    8\timport os\n    9\timport re\n   10\timport shutil\n   11\tfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter\n   12\tfrom mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n   13\tfrom mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n   14\t\n   15\tSYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX = {\n   16\t    \"cc\": 2,\n   17\t    \"vix\": 0,\n   18\t}\n   19\t\n   20\tMODEL_PRICING = {\n   21\t    \"claude-opus-4-6\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n   22\t    \"claude-opus-4-5\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n   23\t    \"claude-opus-4-1\":   {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n   24\t    \"claude-opus-4\":     {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n   25\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n   26\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-5\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n   27\t    \"claude-sonnet-4\":   {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n   28\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5\":  {\"input\": 1e-6,    \"cache_write\": 1.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.10e-6,  \"output\": 5e-6},\n   29\t    \"claude-haiku-3-5\":  {\"input\": 0.80e-6, \"cache_write\": 1e-6,     \"cache_read\": 0.08e-6,  \"output\": 4e-6},\n   30\t}\n   31\t\n   32\t# Sort prefixes longest-first so \"claude-opus-4-5\" matches before \"claude-opus-4\"\n   33\t_SORTED_PREFIXES = sorted(MODEL_PRICING.keys(), key=len, reverse=True)\n   34\t\n   35\t\n   36\tdef count_whitespace_stats(text):\n   37\t    \"\"\"Count line returns and unnecessary spaces in text.\n   38\t\n   39\t    Returns dict with:\n   40\t      - line_returns_count: number of \\\\n characters\n   41\t      - unnecessary_space_count: for each run of 2+ spaces, count len(run) - 1\n   42\t      - total_chars: total character count of the text\n   43\t    \"\"\"\n   44\t    line_returns = text.count(\"\\n\")\n   45\t    unnecessary_spaces = sum(len(m) - 1 for m in re.findall(r\" {2,}\", text))\n   46\t    return {\n   47\t        \"line_returns_count\": line_returns,\n   48\t        \"unnecessary_space_count\": unnecessary_spaces,\n   49\t        \"total_chars\": len(text),\n   50\t    }\n   51\t\n   52\t\n   53\tdef parse_request_body(request_path: str):\n   54\t    \"\"\"Parse the JSON body from a request.json file. Returns the parsed dict or None.\"\"\"\n   55\t    try:\n   56\t        with open(request_path, \"r\") as f:\n   57\t            return json.load(f)\n   58\t    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n   59\t        return None\n   60\t\n   61\t\n   62\tdef get_canonical_model(model_id: str):\n   63\t    \"\"\"Return the canonical model name (without date suffix) or None if unknown.\"\"\"\n   64\t    for prefix in _SORTED_PREFIXES:\n   65\t        if model_id.startswith(prefix):\n   66\t            return prefix\n   67\t    return None\n   68\t\n   69\t\n   70\tdef get_pricing(model_id: str):\n   71\t    \"\"\"Match a model ID (possibly with date suffix) to pricing. Returns pricing dict or None.\"\"\"\n   72\t    canonical = get_canonical_model(model_id)\n   73\t    if canonical:\n   74\t        return MODEL_PRICING[canonical]\n   75\t    return None\n   76\t\n   77\t\n   78\tdef sanitize_path(path: str) -\u003e str:\n   79\t    \"\"\"Turn a URL path into a safe directory name component.\"\"\"\n   80\t    path = path.split(\"?\")[0]\n   81\t    path = path.replace(\"/\", \"_\")\n   82\t    path = path.strip(\"_\")\n   83\t    path = re.sub(r\"[^a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]\", \"\", path)\n   84\t    return path[:80]\n   85\t\n   86\t\n   87\t_REDACTED_HEADERS = {b\"x-api-key\", b\"authorization\"}\n   88\t\n   89\t\n   90\tdef format_headers(headers) -\u003e str:\n   91\t    lines = []\n   92\t    for k, v in headers.fields:\n   93\t        if k.lower() in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n   94\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: [REDACTED]\")\n   95\t        else:\n   96\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: {v}\")\n   97\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n   98\t\n   99\t\n  100\tdef write_request(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n  101\t    req = flow.request\n  102\t    # Write headers file (method+URL line, blank line, headers)\n  103\t    header_lines = [\n  104\t        f\"{req.method} {req.pretty_url}\",\n  105\t        \"\",\n  106\t        format_headers(req.headers),\n  107\t    ]\n  108\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request_headers.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n  109\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(header_lines))\n  110\t    # Write body as JSON (pretty-printed if valid JSON, raw fallback)\n  111\t    body = req.get_text(strict=False)\n  112\t    if body:\n  113\t        try:\n  114\t            parsed = json.loads(body)\n  115\t            body_out = json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n  116\t        except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n  117\t            body_out = body\n  118\t        with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n  119\t            f.write(body_out)\n  120\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n  121\t\n  122\t\n  123\t\n  124\tdef write_response(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n  125\t    resp = flow.response\n  126\t    if resp is None:\n  127\t        return\n  128\t    lines = [\n  129\t        f\"{resp.status_code} {resp.reason}\",\n  130\t        \"\",\n  131\t        format_headers(resp.headers),\n  132\t    ]\n  133\t    body = resp.get_text(strict=False)\n  134\t    if body:\n  135\t        lines += [\"\", body]\n  136\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"response_raw.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n  137\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n  138\t\n  139\t\n  140\tdef extract_stop_reason(response_raw: str) -\u003e str:\n  141\t    \"\"\"Extract stop_reason from SSE message_delta event or non-streaming JSON response.\"\"\"\n  142\t    # Try SSE streaming format\n  143\t    for line in response_raw.splitlines():\n  144\t        line = line.strip()\n  145\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n  146\t            continue\n  147\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n  148\t        if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n  149\t            continue\n  150\t        try:\n  151\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n  152\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n  153\t            reason = delta.get(\"stop_reason\")\n  154\t            if reason:\n  155\t                return reason\n  156\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  157\t            continue\n  158\t\n  159\t    # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response\n  160\t    for line in reversed(response_raw.splitlines()):\n  161\t        line = line.strip()\n  162\t        if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n  163\t            continue\n  164\t        try:\n  165\t            data = json.loads(line)\n  166\t            if data.get(\"type\") == \"message\":\n  167\t                reason = data.get(\"stop_reason\")\n  168\t                if reason:\n  169\t                    return reason\n  170\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  171\t            continue\n  172\t\n  173\t    return \"unknown\"\n  174\t\n  175\t\n  176\tdef redact_flow_files(directory: str):\n  177\t    \"\"\"Redact sensitive headers (API keys) from .flow files in-place.\"\"\"\n  178\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, \"*.flow\")))\n  179\t    if not flow_files:\n  180\t        return\n  181\t\n  182\t    count = 0\n  183\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n  184\t        flows = []\n  185\t        modified = False\n  186\t        try:\n  187\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n  188\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n  189\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n  190\t                    if isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n  191\t                        for header in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n  192\t                            if flow.request.headers.get(header):\n  193\t                                flow.request.headers[header] = \"[REDACTED]\"\n  194\t                                modified = True\n  195\t                    flows.append(flow)\n  196\t        except (FlowReadException, Exception) as e:\n  197\t            print(f\"  Skipping {os.path.basename(filepath)}: {e}\")\n  198\t            continue\n  199\t\n  200\t        if modified:\n  201\t            with open(filepath, \"wb\") as f:\n  202\t                writer = FlowWriter(f)\n  203\t                for flow in flows:\n  204\t                    writer.add(flow)\n  205\t            count += 1\n  206\t\n  207\t    print(f\"\\nRedacted API keys in {count} flow files\")\n  208\t\n  209\t\n  210\tdef _system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name):\n  211\t    \"\"\"Return a short hash of the relevant system prompt, or None.\"\"\"\n  212\t    system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n  213\t    if not system:\n  214\t        return None\n  215\t    index = SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX.get(agent_name, 0)\n  216\t    if index \u003e= len(system):\n  217\t        return None\n  218\t    text = system[index].get(\"text\", \"\")\n  219\t    if not text:\n  220\t        return None\n  221\t    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n  222\t\n  223\t\n  224\tdef export_flows(input_dir: str, output_dir: str):\n  225\t    \"\"\"Export .flow files from input_dir into per-flow directories under output_dir.\n  226\t\n  227\t    Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n  228\t    Steps are delimited by end_turn stop_reason in responses.\n  229\t    \"\"\"\n  230\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(input_dir, \"*.flow\")))\n  231\t    if not flow_files:\n  232\t        print(f\"No *.flow files found in {input_dir}\")\n  233\t        return\n  234\t\n  235\t    total = 0\n  236\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n  237\t        filename = os.path.basename(filepath)\n  238\t        name = os.path.splitext(filename)[0]\n  239\t        file_dir = os.path.join(output_dir, name)\n  240\t        if os.path.exists(file_dir):\n  241\t            shutil.rmtree(file_dir)\n  242\t        os.makedirs(file_dir)\n  243\t        print(f\"Reading {filename}...\")\n  244\t        try:\n  245\t            step_index = 1\n  246\t            request_index = 1\n  247\t            prev_prompt_hash = None\n  248\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n  249\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n  250\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n  251\t                    if not isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n  252\t                        continue\n  253\t\n  254\t                    url = flow.request.pretty_url\n  255\t                    if \"/count_token\" in url:\n  256\t                        continue\n  257\t\n  258\t                    # Parse body to check for quota requests\n  259\t                    body_text = flow.request.get_text(strict=False)\n  260\t                    body_json = None\n  261\t                    if body_text:\n  262\t                        try:\n  263\t                            body_json = json.loads(body_text)\n  264\t                            messages = body_json.get(\"messages\", [])\n  265\t                            system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n  266\t                            if messages and not system:\n  267\t                                first_msg = messages[0]\n  268\t                                content = first_msg.get(\"content\", \"\")\n  269\t                                if isinstance(content, str) and content == \"quota\":\n  270\t                                    continue\n  271\t                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  272\t                            pass\n  273\t\n  274\t                    # For cc: step boundary = system prompt change (checked before writing)\n  275\t                    if name == \"cc\" and body_json is not None:\n  276\t                        prompt_hash = _system_prompt_hash(body_json, name)\n  277\t                        if prompt_hash is not None and prev_prompt_hash is not None and prompt_hash != prev_prompt_hash:\n  278\t                            step_index += 1\n  279\t                            request_index = 1\n  280\t                        if prompt_hash is not None:\n  281\t                            prev_prompt_hash = prompt_hash\n  282\t\n  283\t                    flow_dir = os.path.join(file_dir, str(step_index), str(request_index))\n  284\t                    os.makedirs(flow_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  285\t\n  286\t                    write_request(flow, flow_dir)\n  287\t                    write_response(flow, flow_dir)\n  288\t                    # Write timing data inline\n  289\t                    timing = {}\n  290\t                    if flow.request:\n  291\t                        timing[\"request_start\"] = flow.request.timestamp_start\n  292\t                    if flow.response:\n  293\t                        timing[\"response_end\"] = flow.response.timestamp_end\n  294\t                    with open(os.path.join(flow_dir, \"timing.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n  295\t                        json.dump(timing, f, indent=2)\n  296\t                        f.write(\"\\n\")\n  297\t\n  298\t                    # Extract stop_reason to determine step boundaries\n  299\t                    response_raw = \"\"\n  300\t                    resp = flow.response\n  301\t                    if resp is not None:\n  302\t                        response_raw = resp.get_text(strict=False) or \"\"\n  303\t                    stop_reason = extract_stop_reason(response_raw)\n  304\t\n  305\t                    print(f\"  [step {step_index}, req {request_index}] {flow.request.method} {flow.request.pretty_url} ({stop_reason})\")\n  306\t\n  307\t                    # For vix: step boundary = end_turn stop_reason (checked after writing)\n  308\t                    if name != \"cc\":\n  309\t                        if stop_reason == \"end_turn\":\n  310\t                            step_index += 1\n  311\t                            request_index = 1\n  312\t                        else:\n  313\t                            request_index += 1\n  314\t                    else:\n  315\t                        request_index += 1\n  316\t\n  317\t                    total += 1\n  318\t        except FlowReadException as e:\n  319\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n  320\t        except Exception as e:\n  321\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n  322\t\n  323\t    print(f\"\\nExported {total} flows to {output_dir}\")\n  324\t\n  325\t\n  326\tdef extract_usage(directory: str):\n  327\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, extract token usage from SSE message_delta events into usage.json.\"\"\"\n  328\t    count = 0\n  329\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n  330\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n  331\t            continue\n  332\t\n  333\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n  334\t        usage = None\n  335\t        with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n  336\t            content = f.read()\n  337\t\n  338\t        # Try SSE streaming format: look for message_delta events\n  339\t        for line in content.splitlines():\n  340\t            line = line.strip()\n  341\t            if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n  342\t                continue\n  343\t            payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n  344\t            if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n  345\t                continue\n  346\t            try:\n  347\t                data = json.loads(payload)\n  348\t                usage = data.get(\"usage\")\n  349\t            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  350\t                continue\n  351\t\n  352\t        # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response (single message object)\n  353\t        # The body comes after a blank line following the headers\n  354\t        if usage is None:\n  355\t            # Find the last {...\"type\":\"message\"...} JSON in the content\n  356\t            for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n  357\t                line = line.strip()\n  358\t                if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n  359\t                    continue\n  360\t                try:\n  361\t                    msg = json.loads(line)\n  362\t                    if msg.get(\"type\") == \"message\" and \"usage\" in msg:\n  363\t                        usage = msg[\"usage\"]\n  364\t                        break\n  365\t                except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n  366\t                    continue\n  367\t\n  368\t        if usage is None:\n  369\t            print(f\"  Warning: no usage found in {response_path}\")\n  370\t            continue\n  371\t\n  372\t        # Keep only the token count fields we need\n  373\t        TOKEN_FIELDS = (\"input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\")\n  374\t        usage = {k: v for k, v in usage.items() if k in TOKEN_FIELDS}\n  375\t\n  376\t        # Merge timing data if available\n  377\t        timing_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"timing.json\")\n  378\t        if os.path.exists(timing_path):\n  379\t            with open(timing_path, \"r\") as f:\n  380\t                timing = json.load(f)\n  381\t            request_start = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n  382\t            response_end = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n  383\t            timing_block = {}\n  384\t            if request_start:\n  385\t                timing_block[\"request_start\"] = request_start\n  386\t            if response_end:\n  387\t                timing_block[\"response_end\"] = response_end\n  388\t            if request_start and response_end:\n  389\t                timing_block[\"duration_ms\"] = round((response_end - request_start) * 1000)\n  390\t            if timing_block:\n  391\t                usage[\"timing\"] = timing_block\n  392\t            os.remove(timing_path)\n  393\t\n  394\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n  395\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n  396\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n  397\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n  398\t        count += 1\n  399\t\n  400\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted usage for {count} flows\")\n  401\t\n  402\t\n  403\t\n  404\tdef extract_prompts(directory: str):\n  405\t    \"\"\"Extract system prompt and first user message from request.json files into per-request markdown files.\"\"\"\n  406\t    count = 0\n  407\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n  408\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames:\n  409\t            continue\n  410\t\n  411\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n  412\t\n  413\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n  414\t        if body is None:\n  415\t            print(f\"  Warning: no JSON body found in {request_path}\")\n  416\t            continue\n  417\t\n  418\t        # System prompt: concatenate all text blocks from body[\"system\"]\n  419\t        system = body.get(\"system\")\n  420\t        if system and isinstance(system, list):\n  421\t            texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in system if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n  422\t            system_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n  423\t            if system_text:\n  424\t                with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"system_prompt.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n  425\t                    f.write(system_text)\n  426\t\n  427\t        # First user message: find first message with role==\"user\", concatenate text blocks\n  428\t        messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  429\t        for msg in messages:\n  430\t            if msg.get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n  431\t                content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  432\t                if isinstance(content, list):\n  433\t                    texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in content if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n  434\t                    user_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n  435\t                    if user_text:\n  436\t                        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"first_user_message.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n  437\t                            f.write(user_text)\n  438\t                break\n  439\t\n  440\t        count += 1\n  441\t\n  442\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted prompts for {count} requests\")\n  443\t\n  444\t\n  445\t\n  446\tdef _resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input):\n  447\t    \"\"\"Resolve read_file tool name to compressed/uncompressed variant.\"\"\"\n  448\t    if name == \"read_file\":\n  449\t        mode = tool_input.get(\"mode\", \"original\") if isinstance(tool_input, dict) else \"original\"\n  450\t        return \"read_file_compressed\" if mode == \"compress\" else \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n  451\t    return name\n  452\t\n  453\t\n  454\tdef extract_read_file_whitespace(body):\n  455\t    \"\"\"Extract whitespace stats from read_file/Read tool results in the request body.\"\"\"\n  456\t    ws = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n  457\t\n  458\t    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e tool_name map from assistant messages\n  459\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n  460\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  461\t    for msg in messages:\n  462\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  463\t            continue\n  464\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  465\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  466\t            continue\n  467\t        for block in content:\n  468\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n  469\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n  470\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  471\t\n  472\t    for msg in messages:\n  473\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n  474\t            continue\n  475\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  476\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  477\t            continue\n  478\t        for block in content:\n  479\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n  480\t                continue\n  481\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n  482\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n  483\t            if not (tool_name.startswith(\"read_file\") or tool_name == \"Read\"):\n  484\t                continue\n  485\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n  486\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n  487\t                text_for_ws = result_content\n  488\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n  489\t                text_for_ws = \"\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in result_content)\n  490\t            else:\n  491\t                text_for_ws = \"\"\n  492\t            stats = count_whitespace_stats(text_for_ws)\n  493\t            for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n  494\t                ws[k] += stats[k]\n  495\t\n  496\t    return ws\n  497\t\n  498\t\n  499\tdef categorize_input_sources(body):\n  500\t    \"\"\"Count input characters from tool results and tool use blocks, split by cache position.\n  501\t\n  502\t    Returns: {\n  503\t        \"total_chars\": int,  # total chars of entire request body\n  504\t        \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 1234}, ...},\n  505\t        \"tool_calls\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 567}, ...},\n  506\t    }\n  507\t\n  508\t    Position logic:\n  509\t    - Last user message content ‚Üí cache_write (new content being written to cache)\n  510\t    - Second-to-last message (assistant before last user) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use blocks\n  511\t    - Everything else ‚Üí cache_read\n  512\t    \"\"\"\n  513\t    total_chars = len(json.dumps(body))\n  514\t    tool_results = {}\n  515\t    tool_calls = {}\n  516\t\n  517\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  518\t\n  519\t    # Find last user message index and second-to-last message index\n  520\t    last_user_idx = -1\n  521\t    for i in range(len(messages) - 1, -1, -1):\n  522\t        if messages[i].get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n  523\t            last_user_idx = i\n  524\t            break\n  525\t    second_to_last_idx = last_user_idx - 1 if last_user_idx \u003e 0 else -1\n  526\t\n  527\t    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e tool_name map from assistant messages\n  528\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n  529\t    for msg in messages:\n  530\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  531\t            continue\n  532\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  533\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  534\t            continue\n  535\t        for block in content:\n  536\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n  537\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n  538\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  539\t\n  540\t    # Collect tool_result chars from user messages\n  541\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n  542\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n  543\t            continue\n  544\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  545\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  546\t            continue\n  547\t        is_cache_write = (i == last_user_idx)\n  548\t        for block in content:\n  549\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n  550\t                continue\n  551\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n  552\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n  553\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n  554\t            if tool_name not in tool_results:\n  555\t                tool_results[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n  556\t            if is_cache_write:\n  557\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n  558\t            else:\n  559\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n  560\t\n  561\t    # Collect tool_use chars from assistant messages\n  562\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n  563\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  564\t            continue\n  565\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  566\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  567\t            continue\n  568\t        is_cache_write = (i == second_to_last_idx)\n  569\t        for block in content:\n  570\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n  571\t                continue\n  572\t            tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n  573\t                block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  574\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n  575\t            if tool_name not in tool_calls:\n  576\t                tool_calls[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n  577\t            if is_cache_write:\n  578\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n  579\t            else:\n  580\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n  581\t\n  582\t    return {\"total_chars\": total_chars, \"tool_results\": tool_results, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n  583\t\n  584\t\n  585\tdef categorize_output_sources(response_path):\n  586\t    \"\"\"Count output characters from the actual response (SSE stream or single JSON).\n  587\t\n  588\t    Parses content_block_start/delta/stop events from response_raw.txt.\n  589\t    Returns: {\"llm_text\": int, \"tool_calls\": {\"ToolName\": int, ...}}\n  590\t    \"\"\"\n  591\t    llm_text_chars = 0\n  592\t    tool_calls = {}\n  593\t\n  594\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n  595\t        content = f.read()\n  596\t\n  597\t    # State machine for SSE content blocks\n  598\t    # blocks[index] = {\"type\": \"text\"|\"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"text\": str, \"json\": str}\n  599\t    blocks = {}\n  600\t    found_sse = False\n  601\t\n  602\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n  603\t        line = line.strip()\n  604\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n  605\t            continue\n  606\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n  607\t        try:\n  608\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n  609\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  610\t            continue\n  611\t\n  612\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n  613\t\n  614\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n  615\t            found_sse = True\n  616\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n  617\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n  618\t            blocks[idx] = {\n  619\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n  620\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n  621\t                \"text\": \"\",\n  622\t                \"json\": \"\",\n  623\t            }\n  624\t\n  625\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n  626\t            found_sse = True\n  627\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n  628\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n  629\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n  630\t            if idx in blocks:\n  631\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n  632\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n  633\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n  634\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n  635\t\n  636\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n  637\t            found_sse = True\n  638\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n  639\t            if idx in blocks:\n  640\t                block = blocks[idx]\n  641\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n  642\t                    llm_text_chars += len(block[\"text\"])\n  643\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n  644\t                    try:\n  645\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n  646\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  647\t                        input_data = {}\n  648\t                    tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(block[\"name\"], input_data)\n  649\t                    # Reconstruct full block to count all chars (id, name, type, input)\n  650\t                    full_block = {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data}\n  651\t                    chars = len(json.dumps(full_block))\n  652\t                    tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n  653\t                del blocks[idx]\n  654\t\n  655\t    # Non-streaming fallback: parse single JSON message\n  656\t    if not found_sse:\n  657\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n  658\t            line = line.strip()\n  659\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n  660\t                continue\n  661\t            try:\n  662\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n  663\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n  664\t                    continue\n  665\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n  666\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n  667\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n  668\t                        llm_text_chars += len(block.get(\"text\", \"\"))\n  669\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n  670\t                        tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n  671\t                            block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  672\t                        chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n  673\t                        tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n  674\t                break\n  675\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n  676\t                continue\n  677\t\n  678\t    return {\"llm_text\": llm_text_chars, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n  679\t\n  680\t\n  681\tdef _format_tool_params(input_data):\n  682\t    \"\"\"Format tool input as compact param=value pairs.\"\"\"\n  683\t    parts = []\n  684\t    for key, value in input_data.items():\n  685\t        if isinstance(value, str):\n  686\t            parts.append(f'{key}=\"{value}\"')\n  687\t        else:\n  688\t            parts.append(f\"{key}={json.dumps(value)}\")\n  689\t    return \", \".join(parts)\n  690\t\n  691\t\n  692\tdef parse_response_content(response_path):\n  693\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt into a list of content blocks.\n  694\t\n  695\t    Returns: list of {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": str} or {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"input\": dict}\n  696\t    \"\"\"\n  697\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n  698\t        content = f.read()\n  699\t\n  700\t    # SSE streaming parse\n  701\t    blocks = {}\n  702\t    finished = []\n  703\t    found_sse = False\n  704\t\n  705\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n  706\t        line = line.strip()\n  707\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n  708\t            continue\n  709\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n  710\t        try:\n  711\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n  712\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  713\t            continue\n  714\t\n  715\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n  716\t\n  717\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n  718\t            found_sse = True\n  719\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n  720\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n  721\t            blocks[idx] = {\n  722\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n  723\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n  724\t                \"text\": \"\",\n  725\t                \"json\": \"\",\n  726\t            }\n  727\t\n  728\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n  729\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n  730\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n  731\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n  732\t            if idx in blocks:\n  733\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n  734\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n  735\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n  736\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n  737\t\n  738\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n  739\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n  740\t            if idx in blocks:\n  741\t                block = blocks[idx]\n  742\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n  743\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block[\"text\"]})\n  744\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n  745\t                    try:\n  746\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n  747\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  748\t                        input_data = {}\n  749\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data})\n  750\t                del blocks[idx]\n  751\t\n  752\t    # Non-streaming fallback\n  753\t    if not found_sse:\n  754\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n  755\t            line = line.strip()\n  756\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n  757\t                continue\n  758\t            try:\n  759\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n  760\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n  761\t                    continue\n  762\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n  763\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n  764\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n  765\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block.get(\"text\", \"\")})\n  766\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n  767\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), \"input\": block.get(\"input\", {})})\n  768\t                break\n  769\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n  770\t                continue\n  771\t\n  772\t    return finished\n  773\t\n  774\t\n  775\tdef export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n  776\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt and write a human-readable response_parsed.txt.\n  777\t\n  778\t    Text blocks are output as-is. Tool calls are displayed inline with params.\n  779\t    \"\"\"\n  780\t    blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n  781\t    if not blocks:\n  782\t        return False\n  783\t\n  784\t    lines = []\n  785\t    for block in blocks:\n  786\t        if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n  787\t            lines.append(block[\"text\"])\n  788\t        elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n  789\t            params = _format_tool_params(block[\"input\"])\n  790\t            lines.append(f'\\n[{block[\"name\"]}({params})]\\n')\n  791\t\n  792\t    with open(output_path, \"w\") as f:\n  793\t        f.write(\"\".join(lines))\n  794\t    return True\n  795\t\n  796\t\n  797\tdef export_parsed_responses(directory: str):\n  798\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, export response_parsed.txt for each response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n  799\t    count = 0\n  800\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n  801\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n  802\t            continue\n  803\t\n  804\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n  805\t        output_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_parsed.txt\")\n  806\t\n  807\t        if export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n  808\t            count += 1\n  809\t\n  810\t    print(f\"\\nExported parsed responses for {count} flows\")\n  811\t\n  812\t\n  813\tdef attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing):\n  814\t    \"\"\"Attribute tokens/cost to source categories.\n  815\t\n  816\t    Input side: raw character counts per tool (no token/cost distribution ‚Äî flawed due to caching).\n  817\t    Output side: proportional token/cost distribution (valid since output isn't cached).\n  818\t    \"\"\"\n  819\t    by_source = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n  820\t\n  821\t    # Input: distribute input tokens proportionally using total_chars as denominator\n  822\t    cost_data = usage.get(\"cost\", {})\n  823\t    _ci = cost_data.get(\"input\", {})\n  824\t    _cw = cost_data.get(\"cache_write\", {})\n  825\t    _cr = cost_data.get(\"cache_read\", {})\n  826\t    input_tokens = _ci.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cw.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cr.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  827\t\n  828\t    total_chars = input_sources.get(\"total_chars\", 0)\n  829\t\n  830\t    def _attribute_input_tool(tool_char_dict):\n  831\t        \"\"\"Compute tokens/dollars/chars for a tool given its {cache_write_chars, cache_read_chars}.\"\"\"\n  832\t        cw_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0)\n  833\t        cr_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0)\n  834\t        cw_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cw_chars / total_chars))\n  835\t        cr_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cr_chars / total_chars))\n  836\t        dollars = (\n  837\t            round(cw_tokens * pricing[\"cache_write\"], 6) +\n  838\t            round(cr_tokens * pricing[\"cache_read\"], 6)\n  839\t        )\n  840\t        return {\"tokens\": cw_tokens + cr_tokens, \"dollars\": dollars, \"chars\": cw_chars + cr_chars}\n  841\t\n  842\t    if total_chars \u003e 0 and input_tokens \u003e 0 and pricing:\n  843\t        # Tool results (from user messages)\n  844\t        tool_results = input_sources.get(\"tool_results\", {})\n  845\t        if tool_results:\n  846\t            tr_entry = {}\n  847\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_results.items():\n  848\t                tr_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n  849\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"] = tr_entry\n  850\t\n  851\t        # Tool calls (from assistant messages)\n  852\t        tool_calls_input = input_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n  853\t        if tool_calls_input:\n  854\t            tc_entry = {}\n  855\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_calls_input.items():\n  856\t                tc_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n  857\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n  858\t\n  859\t    # Output: distribute output tokens proportionally by character count\n  860\t    output_cost_entry = cost_data.get(\"output\", {})\n  861\t    output_tokens = output_cost_entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n  862\t    output_dollars = output_cost_entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n  863\t\n  864\t    llm_chars = output_sources.get(\"llm_text\", 0)\n  865\t    tc = output_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n  866\t    tc_total_chars = sum(tc.values())\n  867\t    total_output_chars = llm_chars + tc_total_chars\n  868\t\n  869\t    if total_output_chars \u003e 0 and output_tokens \u003e 0:\n  870\t        # LLM text\n  871\t        llm_frac = llm_chars / total_output_chars\n  872\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"] = {\n  873\t            \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * llm_frac),\n  874\t            \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * llm_frac, 6),\n  875\t            \"chars\": llm_chars,\n  876\t        }\n  877\t\n  878\t        # Tool calls\n  879\t        tc_frac = tc_total_chars / total_output_chars\n  880\t        tc_entry = {\n  881\t            \"__total\": {\n  882\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tc_frac),\n  883\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tc_frac, 6),\n  884\t                \"chars\": tc_total_chars,\n  885\t            }\n  886\t        }\n  887\t        for tool_name, chars in tc.items():\n  888\t            tool_frac = chars / total_output_chars\n  889\t            tc_entry[tool_name] = {\n  890\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tool_frac),\n  891\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tool_frac, 6),\n  892\t                \"chars\": chars,\n  893\t            }\n  894\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n  895\t\n  896\t    return by_source\n  897\t\n  898\t\n  899\tREAD_TOOLS = {\"read_file\", \"Read\", \"read_file_compressed\", \"read_file_uncompressed\"}\n  900\tWRITE_TOOLS = {\"write_file\", \"Write\", \"edit_file\", \"Edit\"}\n  901\t\n  902\t\n  903\t_PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n  904\t\n  905\t\n  906\tdef _get_file_path(input_data):\n  907\t    \"\"\"Extract file path from tool input, checking common key names. Always returns an absolute path.\"\"\"\n  908\t    if not isinstance(input_data, dict):\n  909\t        return None\n  910\t    fp = input_data.get(\"file_path\") or input_data.get(\"path\") or None\n  911\t    if fp and not os.path.isabs(fp):\n  912\t        fp = os.path.join(_PROJECT_ROOT, fp)\n  913\t    return fp\n  914\t\n  915\t\n  916\tdef extract_file_ops(body, response_path):\n  917\t    \"\"\"Extract file operation stats from request body (reads) and response (writes).\n  918\t\n  919\t    Returns: {\n  920\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": int, \"total_read_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n  921\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": int, \"total_write_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n  922\t    }\n  923\t    \"\"\"\n  924\t    # --- Input: files read (from conversation history in request body) ---\n  925\t    read_per_file = {}  # path -\u003e {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n  926\t\n  927\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n  928\t\n  929\t    # Build tool_use_id -\u003e (resolved_name, file_path) map from assistant messages\n  930\t    tool_id_info = {}\n  931\t    for msg in messages:\n  932\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n  933\t            continue\n  934\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  935\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  936\t            continue\n  937\t        for block in content:\n  938\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n  939\t                name = _resolve_read_file_name(block.get(\"name\", \"\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  940\t                if name in READ_TOOLS:\n  941\t                    fp = _get_file_path(block.get(\"input\", {}))\n  942\t                    tool_id_info[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = fp\n  943\t\n  944\t    # Sum chars from tool_result blocks matching read tools\n  945\t    for msg in messages:\n  946\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n  947\t            continue\n  948\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n  949\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n  950\t            continue\n  951\t        for block in content:\n  952\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n  953\t                continue\n  954\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n  955\t            if tool_use_id not in tool_id_info:\n  956\t                continue\n  957\t            fp = tool_id_info[tool_use_id]\n  958\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n  959\t            chars = 0\n  960\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n  961\t                chars = len(result_content)\n  962\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n  963\t                chars = sum(len(b.get(\"text\", \"\")) for b in result_content)\n  964\t            if fp:\n  965\t                if fp not in read_per_file:\n  966\t                    read_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n  967\t                read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tool_use_id] = chars\n  968\t                read_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n  969\t                read_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n  970\t\n  971\t    # --- Output: files written (from response) ---\n  972\t    write_per_file = {}  # path -\u003e {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n  973\t\n  974\t    response_blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n  975\t    for block in response_blocks:\n  976\t        if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n  977\t            continue\n  978\t        name = block.get(\"name\", \"\")\n  979\t        if name not in WRITE_TOOLS:\n  980\t            continue\n  981\t        inp = block.get(\"input\", {})\n  982\t        fp = _get_file_path(inp)\n  983\t        # Sum content chars: \"content\" for Write/write_file, \"new_string\" for Edit/edit_file\n  984\t        chars = 0\n  985\t        if name in (\"Write\", \"write_file\"):\n  986\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"content\", \"\"))\n  987\t        elif name in (\"Edit\", \"edit_file\"):\n  988\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"new_string\", \"\"))\n  989\t        if fp:\n  990\t            block_id = block.get(\"id\", \"\")\n  991\t            if fp not in write_per_file:\n  992\t                write_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n  993\t            write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][block_id] = chars\n  994\t            write_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n  995\t            write_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n  996\t\n  997\t    # Add file_size for each file\n  998\t    for pf in (read_per_file, write_per_file):\n  999\t        for fp in pf:\n 1000\t            try:\n 1001\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = os.path.getsize(fp)\n 1002\t            except OSError:\n 1003\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = None\n 1004\t\n 1005\t    # Derive aggregate scalars from deduplicated per_file data\n 1006\t    unique_files_read = len(read_per_file)\n 1007\t    total_read_chars = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in read_per_file.values())\n 1008\t    unique_files_written = len(write_per_file)\n 1009\t    total_write_chars_dedup = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n 1010\t    total_write_calls = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n 1011\t\n 1012\t    return {\n 1013\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": unique_files_read, \"total_read_chars\": total_read_chars, \"per_file\": read_per_file},\n 1014\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": total_write_calls, \"unique_files_written\": unique_files_written, \"total_write_chars\": total_write_chars_dedup, \"per_file\": write_per_file},\n 1015\t    }\n 1016\t\n 1017\t\n 1018\tdef extract_source_attribution(directory: str):\n 1019\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute source attribution, read_file whitespace, and file ops.\"\"\"\n 1020\t    count = 0\n 1021\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n 1022\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames or \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n 1023\t            continue\n 1024\t\n 1025\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n 1026\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n 1027\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n 1028\t\n 1029\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n 1030\t        if body is None:\n 1031\t            continue\n 1032\t\n 1033\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n 1034\t            usage = json.load(f)\n 1035\t\n 1036\t        # Get model pricing\n 1037\t        model = body.get(\"model\", \"\")\n 1038\t        pricing = get_pricing(model) if model else None\n 1039\t\n 1040\t        # Compute source attribution\n 1041\t        input_sources = categorize_input_sources(body)\n 1042\t        output_sources = categorize_output_sources(response_path)\n 1043\t        by_source = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)\n 1044\t\n 1045\t        usage[\"by_source\"] = by_source\n 1046\t\n 1047\t        # Compute read_file whitespace\n 1048\t        usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n 1049\t\n 1050\t        # Compute file operations\n 1051\t        usage[\"file_ops\"] = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n 1052\t\n 1053\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n 1054\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n 1055\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n 1056\t        count += 1\n 1057\t\n 1058\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted source attribution for {count} flows\")\n 1059\t\n 1060\t\n 1061\tdef calculate_costs(directory: str):\n 1062\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute dollar costs from usage.json and request.json model info.\"\"\"\n 1063\t    count = 0\n 1064\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n 1065\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames:\n 1066\t            continue\n 1067\t\n 1068\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n 1069\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n 1070\t        if body is None:\n 1071\t            continue\n 1072\t\n 1073\t        model = body.get(\"model\")\n 1074\t        if not model:\n 1075\t            continue\n 1076\t\n 1077\t        pricing = get_pricing(model)\n 1078\t        if pricing is None:\n 1079\t            print(f\"  Warning: unknown model '{model}' in {request_path}, skipping cost calculation\")\n 1080\t            continue\n 1081\t\n 1082\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n 1083\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n 1084\t            usage = json.load(f)\n 1085\t\n 1086\t        tokens_input = usage.get(\"input_tokens\", 0)\n 1087\t        tokens_cache_write = usage.get(\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0)\n 1088\t        tokens_cache_read = usage.get(\"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0)\n 1089\t        tokens_output = usage.get(\"output_tokens\", 0)\n 1090\t        tokens_total = tokens_input + tokens_cache_write + tokens_cache_read + tokens_output\n 1091\t\n 1092\t        cost_input = tokens_input * pricing[\"input\"]\n 1093\t        cost_cache_write = tokens_cache_write * pricing[\"cache_write\"]\n 1094\t        cost_cache_read = tokens_cache_read * pricing[\"cache_read\"]\n 1095\t        cost_output = tokens_output * pricing[\"output\"]\n 1096\t        cost_total = cost_input + cost_cache_write + cost_cache_read + cost_output\n 1097\t\n 1098\t        usage[\"cost\"] = {\n 1099\t            \"input\": {\"tokens\": tokens_input, \"dollars\": round(cost_input, 6)},\n 1100\t            \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_write, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_write, 6)},\n 1101\t            \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_read, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_read, 6)},\n 1102\t            \"output\": {\"tokens\": tokens_output, \"dollars\": round(cost_output, 6)},\n 1103\t            \"total\": {\"tokens\": tokens_total, \"dollars\": round(cost_total, 6)},\n 1104\t        }\n 1105\t\n 1106\t        # Remove top-level token keys (now redundant with cost entries)\n 1107\t        for key in (\"input_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\"):\n 1108\t            usage.pop(key, None)\n 1109\t\n 1110\t        canonical = get_canonical_model(model)\n 1111\t        if canonical:\n 1112\t            usage[\"model\"] = canonical\n 1113\t\n 1114\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n 1115\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n 1116\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n 1117\t        count += 1\n 1118\t\n 1119\t    print(f\"\\nCalculated costs for {count} flows\")\n 1120\t\n 1121\t\n 1122\tdef _aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source):\n 1123\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-flow by_source into summary by_source.\n 1124\t\n 1125\t    Input side: sum tool_results {tokens, dollars} dicts.\n 1126\t    Output side: sum token/dollars dicts.\n 1127\t    \"\"\"\n 1128\t    # Input: tool_results and tool_calls are {tokens, dollars} dicts\n 1129\t    flow_input = flow_by_source.get(\"input\", {})\n 1130\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n 1131\t        flow_section = flow_input.get(input_key, {})\n 1132\t        if not flow_section:\n 1133\t            continue\n 1134\t        if input_key not in agg[\"input\"]:\n 1135\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key] = {}\n 1136\t        for tool, entry in flow_section.items():\n 1137\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n 1138\t                continue\n 1139\t            if tool not in agg[\"input\"][input_key]:\n 1140\t                agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n 1141\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n 1142\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n 1143\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n 1144\t\n 1145\t    # Output: token/dollars dicts\n 1146\t    flow_output = flow_by_source.get(\"output\", {})\n 1147\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n 1148\t        entry = flow_output.get(key)\n 1149\t        if entry:\n 1150\t            if key not in agg[\"output\"]:\n 1151\t                agg[\"output\"][key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n 1152\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n 1153\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n 1154\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n 1155\t\n 1156\t    # Tool calls\n 1157\t    flow_tc = flow_output.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n 1158\t    if flow_tc:\n 1159\t        if \"tool_calls\" not in agg[\"output\"]:\n 1160\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = {}\n 1161\t        for tool_key, entry in flow_tc.items():\n 1162\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n 1163\t                continue\n 1164\t            if tool_key not in agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]:\n 1165\t                agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n 1166\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n 1167\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n 1168\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n 1169\t\n 1170\t\n 1171\tdef _round_by_source(agg):\n 1172\t    \"\"\"Round dollar values in the by_source aggregate.\"\"\"\n 1173\t    # Input: round dollars\n 1174\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n 1175\t        section = agg.get(\"input\", {}).get(input_key, {})\n 1176\t        for entry in section.values():\n 1177\t            if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n 1178\t                entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n 1179\t    # Output: round dollars\n 1180\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n 1181\t        entry = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(key)\n 1182\t        if entry:\n 1183\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n 1184\t    tc = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n 1185\t    for entry in tc.values():\n 1186\t        if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n 1187\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n 1188\t\n 1189\t\n 1190\tAGENT_COLORS = {\n 1191\t    \"vix\": \"#7B2FBE\",\n 1192\t    \"cc\": \"#D77656\",\n 1193\t}\n 1194\t\n 1195\t\n 1196\tdef _agent_color(name):\n 1197\t    \"\"\"Return a deterministic hex color for an unknown agent name.\"\"\"\n 1198\t    import hashlib\n 1199\t    h = int(hashlib.md5(name.encode()).hexdigest()[:6], 16)\n 1200\t    return f\"#{h:06x}\"\n 1201\t\n 1202\t\n 1203\tdef summarize_usage(directory: str):\n 1204\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-request usage.json files into a summary usage.json per agent type.\"\"\"\n 1205\t    COST_FIELDS = [\"input\", \"cache_write\", \"cache_read\", \"output\", \"total\"]\n 1206\t\n 1207\t    def empty_bucket():\n 1208\t        bucket = {\"request_count\": 0}\n 1209\t        bucket[\"cost\"] = {f: {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0} for f in COST_FIELDS}\n 1210\t        bucket[\"timing\"] = {\n 1211\t            \"total_duration_ms\": 0,\n 1212\t            \"min_request_start\": None, \"max_response_end\": None,\n 1213\t        }\n 1214\t        return bucket\n 1215\t\n 1216\t    def add_to_bucket(bucket, usage):\n 1217\t        bucket[\"request_count\"] += 1\n 1218\t        cost = usage.get(\"cost\")\n 1219\t        if cost:\n 1220\t            for f in COST_FIELDS:\n 1221\t                entry = cost.get(f, {})\n 1222\t                if isinstance(entry, dict):\n 1223\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n 1224\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n 1225\t        timing = usage.get(\"timing\")\n 1226\t        if timing:\n 1227\t            bucket[\"timing\"][\"total_duration_ms\"] += timing.get(\"duration_ms\", 0)\n 1228\t            rs = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n 1229\t            re_ = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n 1230\t            if rs is not None:\n 1231\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"]\n 1232\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"] = rs if cur is None else min(cur, rs)\n 1233\t            if re_ is not None:\n 1234\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"]\n 1235\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"] = re_ if cur is None else max(cur, re_)\n 1236\t\n 1237\t    def round_costs(bucket):\n 1238\t        for f in COST_FIELDS:\n 1239\t            bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] = round(bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"], 6)\n 1240\t\n 1241\t    count = 0\n 1242\t    for entry in sorted(os.listdir(directory)):\n 1243\t        agent_dir = os.path.join(directory, entry)\n 1244\t        if not os.path.isdir(agent_dir):\n 1245\t            continue\n 1246\t\n 1247\t        # Only process dirs that contain numbered step subdirs\n 1248\t        has_numbered = False\n 1249\t        for sub in os.listdir(agent_dir):\n 1250\t            if sub.isdigit() and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(agent_dir, sub)):\n 1251\t                has_numbered = True\n 1252\t                break\n 1253\t        if not has_numbered:\n 1254\t            continue\n 1255\t\n 1256\t        by_model = {}\n 1257\t        by_step = {}\n 1258\t        total = empty_bucket()\n 1259\t        ws_agg = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n 1260\t        by_source_agg = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n 1261\t        file_ops_agg = {\n 1262\t            \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n 1263\t            \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n 1264\t        }\n 1265\t\n 1266\t        # Iterate step dirs: {agent_dir}/{step_number}/\n 1267\t        for step_sub in sorted(os.listdir(agent_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n 1268\t            if not step_sub.isdigit():\n 1269\t                continue\n 1270\t            step_dir = os.path.join(agent_dir, step_sub)\n 1271\t            if not os.path.isdir(step_dir):\n 1272\t                continue\n 1273\t\n 1274\t            step_key = step_sub  # Use step directory number as key\n 1275\t\n 1276\t            # Iterate request dirs: {step_dir}/{request_number}/usage.json\n 1277\t            for req_sub in sorted(os.listdir(step_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n 1278\t                if not req_sub.isdigit():\n 1279\t                    continue\n 1280\t                usage_path = os.path.join(step_dir, req_sub, \"usage.json\")\n 1281\t                if not os.path.isfile(usage_path):\n 1282\t                    continue\n 1283\t\n 1284\t                with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n 1285\t                    usage = json.load(f)\n 1286\t\n 1287\t                model_name = usage.get(\"model\", \"unknown\")\n 1288\t                if model_name not in by_model:\n 1289\t                    by_model[model_name] = empty_bucket()\n 1290\t                add_to_bucket(by_model[model_name], usage)\n 1291\t\n 1292\t                add_to_bucket(total, usage)\n 1293\t\n 1294\t                # Aggregate by_source\n 1295\t                flow_by_source = usage.get(\"by_source\")\n 1296\t                if flow_by_source:\n 1297\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_source_agg, flow_by_source)\n 1298\t\n 1299\t                # Aggregate read_file whitespace\n 1300\t                flow_ws = usage.get(\"read_file_whitespace\")\n 1301\t                if flow_ws:\n 1302\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n 1303\t                        ws_agg[k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n 1304\t\n 1305\t                # Aggregate file_ops\n 1306\t                flow_file_ops = usage.get(\"file_ops\")\n 1307\t                if flow_file_ops:\n 1308\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n 1309\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n 1310\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n 1311\t                    # Aggregate per-file details (merge tool_ids maps for dedup)\n 1312\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n 1313\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n 1314\t                            agg_pf = file_ops_agg[side][\"per_file\"]\n 1315\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n 1316\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n 1317\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n 1318\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n 1319\t\n 1320\t                # Aggregate per step\n 1321\t                if step_key not in by_step:\n 1322\t                    by_step[step_key] = empty_bucket()\n 1323\t                    by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"] = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n 1324\t                    by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"] = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n 1325\t                    by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"] = {\n 1326\t                        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n 1327\t                        \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n 1328\t                    }\n 1329\t                add_to_bucket(by_step[step_key], usage)\n 1330\t                if flow_by_source:\n 1331\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"], flow_by_source)\n 1332\t                if flow_ws:\n 1333\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n 1334\t                        by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"][k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n 1335\t                if flow_file_ops:\n 1336\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n 1337\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n 1338\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n 1339\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n 1340\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n 1341\t                            agg_pf = by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"][side][\"per_file\"]\n 1342\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n 1343\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n 1344\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n 1345\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n 1346\t\n 1347\t        round_costs(total)\n 1348\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n 1349\t            round_costs(bucket)\n 1350\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n 1351\t            round_costs(bucket)\n 1352\t            if \"by_source\" in bucket:\n 1353\t                _round_by_source(bucket[\"by_source\"])\n 1354\t        _round_by_source(by_source_agg)\n 1355\t\n 1356\t        # Finalize file_ops: convert tool_ids maps to calls/chars, recompute scalars\n 1357\t        def _finalize_file_ops(fops):\n 1358\t            for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n 1359\t                pf = fops[side][\"per_file\"]\n 1360\t                for fp in pf:\n 1361\t                    pf[fp][\"calls\"] = len(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}))\n 1362\t                    pf[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}).values())\n 1363\t                    pf[fp].pop(\"tool_ids\", None)\n 1364\t            fops[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] = len(fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"])\n 1365\t            fops[\"input\"][\"total_read_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n 1366\t            fops[\"output\"][\"unique_files_written\"] = len(fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"])\n 1367\t            fops[\"output\"][\"files_written\"] = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n 1368\t            fops[\"output\"][\"total_write_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n 1369\t\n 1370\t        _finalize_file_ops(file_ops_agg)\n 1371\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n 1372\t            if \"file_ops\" in bucket:\n 1373\t                _finalize_file_ops(bucket[\"file_ops\"])\n 1374\t\n 1375\t        # Finalize timing for each bucket\n 1376\t        def _finalize_timing(bucket):\n 1377\t            t = bucket[\"timing\"]\n 1378\t            req_count = bucket[\"request_count\"]\n 1379\t            mn = t.pop(\"min_request_start\", None)\n 1380\t            mx = t.pop(\"max_response_end\", None)\n 1381\t            if mn is not None and mx is not None:\n 1382\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = round((mx - mn) * 1000)\n 1383\t            else:\n 1384\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = 0\n 1385\t            t[\"avg_duration_ms\"] = round(t[\"total_duration_ms\"] / req_count) if req_count \u003e 0 else 0\n 1386\t\n 1387\t        _finalize_timing(total)\n 1388\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n 1389\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n 1390\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n 1391\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n 1392\t\n 1393\t        total[\"file_ops\"] = file_ops_agg\n 1394\t        summary = {\"title\": entry, \"color\": AGENT_COLORS.get(entry, _agent_color(entry)), \"by_model\": by_model, \"by_step\": by_step, \"by_source\": by_source_agg, \"read_file_whitespace\": ws_agg, \"total\": total}\n 1395\t        summary_path = os.path.join(agent_dir, \"usage.json\")\n 1396\t        with open(summary_path, \"w\") as f:\n 1397\t            json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n 1398\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n 1399\t        count += 1\n 1400\t        print(f\"  Wrote summary: {summary_path} ({total['request_count']} requests)\")\n 1401\t\n 1402\t    print(f\"\\nSummarized usage for {count} agent types\")\n 1403\t\n 1404\t\n 1405\tdef main():\n 1406\t    script_dir = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n 1407\t    data_dir = os.path.join(script_dir, \"data\")\n 1408\t\n 1409\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Export mitmproxy flow files to text.\")\n 1410\t    parser.add_argument(\"--input-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Directory containing *.flow files (default: data/ next to script)\")\n 1411\t    parser.add_argument(\"--output-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Output directory for exported flows (default: data/ next to script)\")\n 1412\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n 1413\t\n 1414\t    input_dir = args.input_directory\n 1415\t    output_dir = args.output_directory\n 1416\t    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n 1417\t\n 1418\t    redact_flow_files(input_dir)\n 1419\t    export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)\n 1420\t    extract_usage(output_dir)\n 1421\t    export_parsed_responses(output_dir)\n 1422\t    extract_prompts(output_dir)\n 1423\t    calculate_costs(output_dir)\n 1424\t    extract_source_attribution(output_dir)\n 1425\t    summarize_usage(output_dir)\n 1426\t\n 1427\t\n 1428\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n 1429\t    main()\n 1430\t","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"Now let me also read the test file to understand what's being tested:","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01DtRDMrTWPF3Vdsbb1seQyy","input":{"path":"/workspace/test_export_flows.py","reason":"Need to understand all the names that tests access via ef.X to ensure all re-exports are correct"},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DtRDMrTWPF3Vdsbb1seQyy","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"    1\t\"\"\"Comprehensive test suite for export_flows.py ‚Äî targets 80%+ code coverage.\"\"\"\n    2\t\n    3\timport json\n    4\timport os\n    5\tfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock, mock_open, patch\n    6\t\n    7\timport pytest\n    8\t\n    9\timport export_flows as ef\n   10\t\n   11\t\n   12\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   13\t# count_whitespace_stats\n   14\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   15\tclass TestCountWhitespaceStats:\n   16\t    def test_empty_string(self):\n   17\t        assert ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"\") == {\n   18\t            \"line_returns_count\": 0,\n   19\t            \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0,\n   20\t            \"total_chars\": 0,\n   21\t        }\n   22\t\n   23\t    def test_no_whitespace(self):\n   24\t        assert ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"abc\") == {\n   25\t            \"line_returns_count\": 0,\n   26\t            \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0,\n   27\t            \"total_chars\": 3,\n   28\t        }\n   29\t\n   30\t    def test_line_returns(self):\n   31\t        result = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a\\nb\\nc\\n\")\n   32\t        assert result[\"line_returns_count\"] == 3\n   33\t\n   34\t    def test_unnecessary_spaces(self):\n   35\t        # \"a  b   c\" -\u003e run of 2 (excess 1) + run of 3 (excess 2) = 3\n   36\t        result = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a  b   c\")\n   37\t        assert result[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 3\n   38\t\n   39\t    def test_single_spaces_not_counted(self):\n   40\t        result = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"a b c\")\n   41\t        assert result[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 0\n   42\t\n   43\t    def test_mixed(self):\n   44\t        result = ef.count_whitespace_stats(\"hello  world\\n  foo\\n\")\n   45\t        assert result[\"line_returns_count\"] == 2\n   46\t        assert result[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1 + 1  # \"  \" twice\n   47\t        assert result[\"total_chars\"] == len(\"hello  world\\n  foo\\n\")\n   48\t\n   49\t\n   50\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   51\t# get_canonical_model / get_pricing\n   52\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   53\tclass TestGetCanonicalModel:\n   54\t    def test_exact_match(self):\n   55\t        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-sonnet-4\") == \"claude-sonnet-4\"\n   56\t\n   57\t    def test_with_date_suffix(self):\n   58\t        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-opus-4-5-20250101\") == \"claude-opus-4-5\"\n   59\t\n   60\t    def test_longer_prefix_wins(self):\n   61\t        # \"claude-opus-4-5\" should match before \"claude-opus-4\"\n   62\t        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"claude-opus-4-5\") == \"claude-opus-4-5\"\n   63\t\n   64\t    def test_unknown_model(self):\n   65\t        assert ef.get_canonical_model(\"gpt-4\") is None\n   66\t\n   67\t\n   68\tclass TestGetPricing:\n   69\t    def test_known_model(self):\n   70\t        p = ef.get_pricing(\"claude-sonnet-4-6\")\n   71\t        assert p is not None\n   72\t        assert \"input\" in p and \"output\" in p\n   73\t\n   74\t    def test_with_suffix(self):\n   75\t        p = ef.get_pricing(\"claude-haiku-3-5-20250101\")\n   76\t        assert p is not None\n   77\t\n   78\t    def test_unknown(self):\n   79\t        assert ef.get_pricing(\"unknown-model\") is None\n   80\t\n   81\t\n   82\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   83\t# sanitize_path\n   84\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   85\tclass TestSanitizePath:\n   86\t    def test_simple(self):\n   87\t        assert ef.sanitize_path(\"/v1/messages\") == \"v1_messages\"\n   88\t\n   89\t    def test_strips_query_string(self):\n   90\t        assert ef.sanitize_path(\"/api/foo?bar=1\") == \"api_foo\"\n   91\t\n   92\t    def test_removes_special_chars(self):\n   93\t        assert ef.sanitize_path(\"/a/b.c!d\") == \"a_bcd\"\n   94\t\n   95\t    def test_truncates_long_path(self):\n   96\t        long = \"/a\" * 100\n   97\t        assert len(ef.sanitize_path(long)) \u003c= 80\n   98\t\n   99\t    def test_empty(self):\n  100\t        assert ef.sanitize_path(\"\") == \"\"\n  101\t\n  102\t\n  103\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  104\t# extract_stop_reason\n  105\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  106\tclass TestExtractStopReason:\n  107\t    def test_sse_message_delta(self):\n  108\t        raw = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"}}\\n'\n  109\t        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"end_turn\"\n  110\t\n  111\t    def test_sse_message_delta_with_spaces(self):\n  112\t        raw = 'data: {\"type\": \"message_delta\", \"delta\": {\"stop_reason\": \"tool_use\"}}\\n'\n  113\t        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"tool_use\"\n  114\t\n  115\t    def test_non_streaming_fallback(self):\n  116\t        raw = '{\"type\": \"message\", \"stop_reason\": \"max_tokens\"}\\n'\n  117\t        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"max_tokens\"\n  118\t\n  119\t    def test_unknown_when_no_match(self):\n  120\t        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(\"no data here\") == \"unknown\"\n  121\t\n  122\t    def test_ignores_non_data_lines(self):\n  123\t        raw = \"event: message_delta\\nfoo bar\\n\"\n  124\t        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"unknown\"\n  125\t\n  126\t    def test_invalid_json_in_sse(self):\n  127\t        raw = \"data: {not json\\ndata: also not\\n\"\n  128\t        assert ef.extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"unknown\"\n  129\t\n  130\t\n  131\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  132\t# _resolve_read_file_name\n  133\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  134\tclass TestResolveReadFileName:\n  135\t    def test_non_read_file(self):\n  136\t        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"Write\", {}) == \"Write\"\n  137\t\n  138\t    def test_read_file_default(self):\n  139\t        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {}) == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n  140\t\n  141\t    def test_read_file_compress(self):\n  142\t        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {\"mode\": \"compress\"}) == \"read_file_compressed\"\n  143\t\n  144\t    def test_read_file_original(self):\n  145\t        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {\"mode\": \"original\"}) == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n  146\t\n  147\t    def test_read_file_non_dict_input(self):\n  148\t        assert ef._resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", \"string\") == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n  149\t\n  150\t\n  151\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  152\t# _format_tool_params\n  153\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  154\tclass TestFormatToolParams:\n  155\t    def test_string_values(self):\n  156\t        result = ef._format_tool_params({\"path\": \"/tmp/foo\"})\n  157\t        assert result == 'path=\"/tmp/foo\"'\n  158\t\n  159\t    def test_non_string_values(self):\n  160\t        result = ef._format_tool_params({\"count\": 5})\n  161\t        assert result == \"count=5\"\n  162\t\n  163\t    def test_mixed(self):\n  164\t        result = ef._format_tool_params({\"file\": \"a.py\", \"line\": 10})\n  165\t        assert 'file=\"a.py\"' in result\n  166\t        assert \"line=10\" in result\n  167\t\n  168\t    def test_empty(self):\n  169\t        assert ef._format_tool_params({}) == \"\"\n  170\t\n  171\t\n  172\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  173\t# format_headers\n  174\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  175\tclass TestFormatHeaders:\n  176\t    def test_normal_headers(self):\n  177\t        headers = MagicMock()\n  178\t        headers.fields = [\n  179\t            (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n  180\t            (b\"accept\", b\"*/*\"),\n  181\t        ]\n  182\t        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n  183\t        assert \"content-type\" in result\n  184\t        assert \"application/json\" in result\n  185\t\n  186\t    def test_redacted_headers(self):\n  187\t        headers = MagicMock()\n  188\t        headers.fields = [\n  189\t            (b\"x-api-key\", b\"secret123\"),\n  190\t            (b\"authorization\", b\"Bearer tok\"),\n  191\t            (b\"host\", b\"example.com\"),\n  192\t        ]\n  193\t        result = ef.format_headers(headers)\n  194\t        assert \"[REDACTED]\" in result\n  195\t        assert \"secret123\" not in result\n  196\t        assert \"Bearer tok\" not in result\n  197\t        assert \"example.com\" in result\n  198\t\n  199\t\n  200\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  201\t# parse_request_body\n  202\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  203\tclass TestParseRequestBody:\n  204\t    def test_valid_json(self, tmp_path):\n  205\t        p = tmp_path / \"req.json\"\n  206\t        p.write_text('{\"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\"}')\n  207\t        result = ef.parse_request_body(str(p))\n  208\t        assert result == {\"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\"}\n  209\t\n  210\t    def test_invalid_json(self, tmp_path):\n  211\t        p = tmp_path / \"req.json\"\n  212\t        p.write_text(\"not json\")\n  213\t        assert ef.parse_request_body(str(p)) is None\n  214\t\n  215\t    def test_empty_file(self, tmp_path):\n  216\t        p = tmp_path / \"req.json\"\n  217\t        p.write_text(\"\")\n  218\t        assert ef.parse_request_body(str(p)) is None\n  219\t\n  220\t\n  221\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  222\t# _get_file_path\n  223\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  224\tclass TestGetFilePath:\n  225\t    def test_file_path_key(self):\n  226\t        result = ef._get_file_path({\"file_path\": \"/abs/path.py\"})\n  227\t        assert result == \"/abs/path.py\"\n  228\t\n  229\t    def test_path_key(self):\n  230\t        result = ef._get_file_path({\"path\": \"/abs/other.py\"})\n  231\t        assert result == \"/abs/other.py\"\n  232\t\n  233\t    def test_relative_path(self):\n  234\t        result = ef._get_file_path({\"file_path\": \"relative/path.py\"})\n  235\t        assert os.path.isabs(result)\n  236\t\n  237\t    def test_no_path(self):\n  238\t        assert ef._get_file_path({\"content\": \"foo\"}) is None\n  239\t\n  240\t    def test_non_dict(self):\n  241\t        assert ef._get_file_path(\"string\") is None\n  242\t\n  243\t\n  244\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  245\t# _agent_color\n  246\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  247\tclass TestAgentColor:\n  248\t    def test_returns_hex(self):\n  249\t        c = ef._agent_color(\"test\")\n  250\t        assert c.startswith(\"#\")\n  251\t        assert len(c) == 7\n  252\t\n  253\t    def test_deterministic(self):\n  254\t        assert ef._agent_color(\"abc\") == ef._agent_color(\"abc\")\n  255\t\n  256\t    def test_different_names_different_colors(self):\n  257\t        # Not guaranteed but extremely likely\n  258\t        assert ef._agent_color(\"agent1\") != ef._agent_color(\"agent2\")\n  259\t\n  260\t\n  261\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  262\t# _system_prompt_hash\n  263\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  264\tclass TestSystemPromptHash:\n  265\t    def test_no_system(self):\n  266\t        assert ef._system_prompt_hash({\"messages\": []}, \"vix\") is None\n  267\t\n  268\t    def test_index_out_of_range(self):\n  269\t        assert ef._system_prompt_hash({\"system\": [{\"text\": \"hi\"}]}, \"cc\") is None  # cc index=2\n  270\t\n  271\t    def test_empty_text(self):\n  272\t        assert ef._system_prompt_hash({\"system\": [{\"text\": \"\"}]}, \"vix\") is None\n  273\t\n  274\t    def test_valid(self):\n  275\t        body = {\"system\": [{\"text\": \"hello\"}, {\"text\": \"world\"}, {\"text\": \"third\"}]}\n  276\t        h = ef._system_prompt_hash(body, \"cc\")  # index 2\n  277\t        assert h is not None\n  278\t        assert len(h) == 12\n  279\t\n  280\t\n  281\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  282\t# write_request / write_response\n  283\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  284\tclass TestWriteRequest:\n  285\t    def test_writes_files(self, tmp_path):\n  286\t        flow = MagicMock()\n  287\t        flow.request.method = \"POST\"\n  288\t        flow.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.example.com/v1/messages\"\n  289\t        flow.request.headers.fields = [(b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\")]\n  290\t        flow.request.get_text.return_value = '{\"model\": \"test\"}'\n  291\t\n  292\t        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n  293\t\n  294\t        headers_file = tmp_path / \"request_headers.txt\"\n  295\t        assert headers_file.exists()\n  296\t        assert \"POST\" in headers_file.read_text()\n  297\t\n  298\t        body_file = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n  299\t        assert body_file.exists()\n  300\t        content = json.loads(body_file.read_text())\n  301\t        assert content[\"model\"] == \"test\"\n  302\t\n  303\t    def test_no_body(self, tmp_path):\n  304\t        flow = MagicMock()\n  305\t        flow.request.method = \"GET\"\n  306\t        flow.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.example.com/\"\n  307\t        flow.request.headers.fields = []\n  308\t        flow.request.get_text.return_value = \"\"\n  309\t\n  310\t        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n  311\t        assert (tmp_path / \"request_headers.txt\").exists()\n  312\t        assert not (tmp_path / \"request.json\").exists()\n  313\t\n  314\t    def test_non_json_body(self, tmp_path):\n  315\t        flow = MagicMock()\n  316\t        flow.request.method = \"POST\"\n  317\t        flow.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.example.com/\"\n  318\t        flow.request.headers.fields = []\n  319\t        flow.request.get_text.return_value = \"not json body\"\n  320\t\n  321\t        ef.write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n  322\t        body_file = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n  323\t        assert body_file.exists()\n  324\t        assert body_file.read_text().strip() == \"not json body\"\n  325\t\n  326\t\n  327\tclass TestWriteResponse:\n  328\t    def test_writes_response(self, tmp_path):\n  329\t        flow = MagicMock()\n  330\t        flow.response.status_code = 200\n  331\t        flow.response.reason = \"OK\"\n  332\t        flow.response.headers.fields = [(b\"content-type\", b\"text/plain\")]\n  333\t        flow.response.get_text.return_value = \"hello\"\n  334\t\n  335\t        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n  336\t        resp_file = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  337\t        assert resp_file.exists()\n  338\t        text = resp_file.read_text()\n  339\t        assert \"200 OK\" in text\n  340\t        assert \"hello\" in text\n  341\t\n  342\t    def test_no_response(self, tmp_path):\n  343\t        flow = MagicMock()\n  344\t        flow.response = None\n  345\t        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n  346\t        assert not (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").exists()\n  347\t\n  348\t    def test_no_body(self, tmp_path):\n  349\t        flow = MagicMock()\n  350\t        flow.response.status_code = 204\n  351\t        flow.response.reason = \"No Content\"\n  352\t        flow.response.headers.fields = []\n  353\t        flow.response.get_text.return_value = \"\"\n  354\t\n  355\t        ef.write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n  356\t        text = (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").read_text()\n  357\t        assert \"204\" in text\n  358\t\n  359\t\n  360\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  361\t# extract_stop_reason edge cases tested above\n  362\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  363\t\n  364\t\n  365\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  366\t# parse_response_content\n  367\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  368\tclass TestParseResponseContent:\n  369\t    def test_sse_text_block(self, tmp_path):\n  370\t        lines = [\n  371\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\"}}',\n  372\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"Hello\"}}',\n  373\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}',\n  374\t        ]\n  375\t        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  376\t        p.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n  377\t        result = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n  378\t        assert len(result) == 1\n  379\t        assert result[0][\"type\"] == \"text\"\n  380\t        assert result[0][\"text\"] == \"Hello\"\n  381\t\n  382\t    def test_sse_tool_use_block(self, tmp_path):\n  383\t        lines = [\n  384\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Read\"}}',\n  385\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{\\\\\"file_path\\\\\":\\\\\"/tmp/f\\\\\"}\"}}',\n  386\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}',\n  387\t        ]\n  388\t        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  389\t        p.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n  390\t        result = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n  391\t        assert len(result) == 1\n  392\t        assert result[0][\"type\"] == \"tool_use\"\n  393\t        assert result[0][\"name\"] == \"Read\"\n  394\t\n  395\t    def test_non_streaming_fallback(self, tmp_path):\n  396\t        msg = {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hi\"}]}\n  397\t        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  398\t        p.write_text(\"200 OK\\n\\n\" + json.dumps(msg))\n  399\t        result = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n  400\t        assert len(result) == 1\n  401\t        assert result[0][\"text\"] == \"Hi\"\n  402\t\n  403\t    def test_empty_response(self, tmp_path):\n  404\t        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  405\t        p.write_text(\"200 OK\\n\\nno json here\")\n  406\t        result = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n  407\t        assert result == []\n  408\t\n  409\t    def test_non_streaming_tool_use(self, tmp_path):\n  410\t        msg = {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Write\", \"input\": {\"content\": \"x\"}}]}\n  411\t        p = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  412\t        p.write_text(json.dumps(msg))\n  413\t        result = ef.parse_response_content(str(p))\n  414\t        assert len(result) == 1\n  415\t        assert result[0][\"type\"] == \"tool_use\"\n  416\t        assert result[0][\"name\"] == \"Write\"\n  417\t\n  418\t\n  419\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  420\t# export_parsed_response\n  421\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  422\tclass TestExportParsedResponse:\n  423\t    def test_text_and_tool_blocks(self, tmp_path):\n  424\t        lines = [\n  425\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\"}}',\n  426\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"Thinking...\"}}',\n  427\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}',\n  428\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":1,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Read\"}}',\n  429\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{\\\\\"path\\\\\": \\\\\"/x\\\\\"}\"}}',\n  430\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":1}',\n  431\t        ]\n  432\t        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  433\t        resp.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n  434\t        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n  435\t        result = ef.export_parsed_response(str(resp), str(out))\n  436\t        assert result is True\n  437\t        text = out.read_text()\n  438\t        assert \"Thinking...\" in text\n  439\t        assert \"[Read(\" in text\n  440\t\n  441\t    def test_empty_returns_false(self, tmp_path):\n  442\t        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  443\t        resp.write_text(\"nothing useful\")\n  444\t        out = tmp_path / \"parsed.txt\"\n  445\t        assert ef.export_parsed_response(str(resp), str(out)) is False\n  446\t\n  447\t\n  448\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  449\t# categorize_output_sources\n  450\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  451\tclass TestCategorizeOutputSources:\n  452\t    def test_sse_text_and_tool(self, tmp_path):\n  453\t        lines = [\n  454\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\"}}',\n  455\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"Hello world\"}}',\n  456\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}',\n  457\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":1,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Write\"}}',\n  458\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{\\\\\"content\\\\\": \\\\\"x\\\\\"}\"}}',\n  459\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":1}',\n  460\t        ]\n  461\t        p = tmp_path / \"resp.txt\"\n  462\t        p.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n  463\t        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n  464\t        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == len(\"Hello world\")\n  465\t        assert \"Write\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n  466\t\n  467\t    def test_non_streaming(self, tmp_path):\n  468\t        msg = {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"abc\"}]}\n  469\t        p = tmp_path / \"resp.txt\"\n  470\t        p.write_text(json.dumps(msg))\n  471\t        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n  472\t        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == 3\n  473\t\n  474\t    def test_empty(self, tmp_path):\n  475\t        p = tmp_path / \"resp.txt\"\n  476\t        p.write_text(\"nothing\")\n  477\t        result = ef.categorize_output_sources(str(p))\n  478\t        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == 0\n  479\t        assert result[\"tool_calls\"] == {}\n  480\t\n  481\t\n  482\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  483\t# extract_read_file_whitespace\n  484\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  485\tclass TestExtractReadFileWhitespace:\n  486\t    def test_no_read_tools(self):\n  487\t        body = {\"messages\": []}\n  488\t        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n  489\t        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == 0\n  490\t\n  491\t    def test_with_read_tool_result(self):\n  492\t        body = {\n  493\t            \"messages\": [\n  494\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  495\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t1\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {}}\n  496\t                ]},\n  497\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  498\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"t1\", \"content\": \"line1\\nline2  extra\"}\n  499\t                ]},\n  500\t            ]\n  501\t        }\n  502\t        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n  503\t        assert ws[\"line_returns_count\"] == 1\n  504\t        assert ws[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1\n  505\t        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == len(\"line1\\nline2  extra\")\n  506\t\n  507\t    def test_list_content_in_tool_result(self):\n  508\t        body = {\n  509\t            \"messages\": [\n  510\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  511\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t1\", \"name\": \"read_file\", \"input\": {\"mode\": \"compress\"}}\n  512\t                ]},\n  513\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  514\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"t1\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"abc  def\"}]}\n  515\t                ]},\n  516\t            ]\n  517\t        }\n  518\t        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n  519\t        assert ws[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1\n  520\t\n  521\t    def test_skips_non_read_tools(self):\n  522\t        body = {\n  523\t            \"messages\": [\n  524\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  525\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t1\", \"name\": \"Write\", \"input\": {}}\n  526\t                ]},\n  527\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  528\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"t1\", \"content\": \"lots  of  spaces\"}\n  529\t                ]},\n  530\t            ]\n  531\t        }\n  532\t        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n  533\t        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == 0\n  534\t\n  535\t    def test_non_list_content_in_messages(self):\n  536\t        body = {\n  537\t            \"messages\": [\n  538\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"plain string\"},\n  539\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"also plain\"},\n  540\t            ]\n  541\t        }\n  542\t        ws = ef.extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n  543\t        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == 0\n  544\t\n  545\t\n  546\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  547\t# categorize_input_sources\n  548\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  549\tclass TestCategorizeInputSources:\n  550\t    def test_empty_messages(self):\n  551\t        body = {\"messages\": []}\n  552\t        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n  553\t        assert result[\"total_chars\"] \u003e 0  # json.dumps of body\n  554\t        assert result[\"tool_results\"] == {}\n  555\t        assert result[\"tool_calls\"] == {}\n  556\t\n  557\t    def test_tool_result_in_last_user_msg_is_cache_write(self):\n  558\t        body = {\n  559\t            \"messages\": [\n  560\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  561\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t1\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {}}\n  562\t                ]},\n  563\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  564\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"t1\", \"content\": \"file contents\"}\n  565\t                ]},\n  566\t            ]\n  567\t        }\n  568\t        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n  569\t        assert \"Read\" in result[\"tool_results\"]\n  570\t        assert result[\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"cache_write_chars\"] \u003e 0\n  571\t\n  572\t    def test_tool_result_in_earlier_user_msg_is_cache_read(self):\n  573\t        body = {\n  574\t            \"messages\": [\n  575\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  576\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t1\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {}}\n  577\t                ]},\n  578\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  579\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"t1\", \"content\": \"old content\"}\n  580\t                ]},\n  581\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  582\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t2\", \"name\": \"Write\", \"input\": {}}\n  583\t                ]},\n  584\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  585\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"t2\", \"content\": \"ok\"}\n  586\t                ]},\n  587\t            ]\n  588\t        }\n  589\t        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n  590\t        assert result[\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"cache_read_chars\"] \u003e 0\n  591\t        assert result[\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"cache_write_chars\"] == 0\n  592\t\n  593\t    def test_tool_use_in_second_to_last_is_cache_write(self):\n  594\t        body = {\n  595\t            \"messages\": [\n  596\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  597\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"t1\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/x\"}}\n  598\t                ]},\n  599\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  600\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"t1\", \"content\": \"data\"}\n  601\t                ]},\n  602\t            ]\n  603\t        }\n  604\t        result = ef.categorize_input_sources(body)\n  605\t        # The assistant message at index 0 is second_to_last (last_user_idx=1, so stl=0)\n  606\t        assert \"Read\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n  607\t        assert result[\"tool_calls\"][\"Read\"][\"cache_write_chars\"] \u003e 0\n  608\t\n  609\t\n  610\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  611\t# attribute_tokens\n  612\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  613\tclass TestAttributeTokens:\n  614\t    def test_basic_attribution(self):\n  615\t        input_sources = {\n  616\t            \"total_chars\": 1000,\n  617\t            \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 500, \"cache_read_chars\": 200}},\n  618\t            \"tool_calls\": {},\n  619\t        }\n  620\t        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 80, \"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": 20}}\n  621\t        usage = {\n  622\t            \"cost\": {\n  623\t                \"input\": {\"tokens\": 100, \"dollars\": 0.001},\n  624\t                \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": 200, \"dollars\": 0.002},\n  625\t                \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": 50, \"dollars\": 0.0005},\n  626\t                \"output\": {\"tokens\": 50, \"dollars\": 0.01},\n  627\t            }\n  628\t        }\n  629\t        pricing = ef.MODEL_PRICING[\"claude-sonnet-4\"]\n  630\t        result = ef.attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)\n  631\t        assert \"input\" in result\n  632\t        assert \"output\" in result\n  633\t        assert result[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"tokens\"] \u003e 0\n  634\t\n  635\t    def test_zero_chars(self):\n  636\t        result = ef.attribute_tokens(\n  637\t            {\"total_chars\": 0, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n  638\t            {\"llm_text\": 0, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n  639\t            {\"cost\": {}},\n  640\t            None,\n  641\t        )\n  642\t        assert result[\"input\"] == {}\n  643\t        assert result[\"output\"] == {}\n  644\t\n  645\t    def test_no_output_tokens(self):\n  646\t        result = ef.attribute_tokens(\n  647\t            {\"total_chars\": 100, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n  648\t            {\"llm_text\": 50, \"tool_calls\": {}},\n  649\t            {\"cost\": {\"output\": {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0}}},\n  650\t            None,\n  651\t        )\n  652\t        assert \"llm_text\" not in result[\"output\"]\n  653\t\n  654\t\n  655\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  656\t# _aggregate_by_source / _round_by_source\n  657\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  658\tclass TestAggregateBySource:\n  659\t    def test_aggregates_input_tool_results(self):\n  660\t        agg = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n  661\t        flow = {\n  662\t            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 10, \"dollars\": 0.001, \"chars\": 100}}},\n  663\t            \"output\": {},\n  664\t        }\n  665\t        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n  666\t        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 10\n  667\t\n  668\t        # Aggregate again\n  669\t        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n  670\t        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 20\n  671\t\n  672\t    def test_aggregates_output(self):\n  673\t        agg = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n  674\t        flow = {\n  675\t            \"input\": {},\n  676\t            \"output\": {\n  677\t                \"llm_text\": {\"tokens\": 5, \"dollars\": 0.01, \"chars\": 50},\n  678\t                \"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": {\"tokens\": 2, \"dollars\": 0.005, \"chars\": 20}},\n  679\t            },\n  680\t        }\n  681\t        ef._aggregate_by_source(agg, flow)\n  682\t        assert agg[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"tokens\"] == 5\n  683\t        assert agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][\"Write\"][\"tokens\"] == 2\n  684\t\n  685\t\n  686\tclass TestRoundBySource:\n  687\t    def test_rounds_dollars(self):\n  688\t        agg = {\n  689\t            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 10, \"dollars\": 0.0011111111, \"chars\": 100}}},\n  690\t            \"output\": {\n  691\t                \"llm_text\": {\"tokens\": 5, \"dollars\": 0.0022222222, \"chars\": 50},\n  692\t                \"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": {\"tokens\": 2, \"dollars\": 0.0033333333, \"chars\": 20}},\n  693\t            },\n  694\t        }\n  695\t        ef._round_by_source(agg)\n  696\t        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.0011111111, 6)\n  697\t        assert agg[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.0022222222, 6)\n  698\t\n  699\t\n  700\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  701\t# extract_usage (filesystem-based)\n  702\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  703\tclass TestExtractUsage:\n  704\t    def test_sse_usage(self, tmp_path):\n  705\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  706\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  707\t\n  708\t        # Write SSE response with message_delta usage\n  709\t        sse = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":100,\"output_tokens\":50,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":10,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":5,\"extra_field\":1}}\\n'\n  710\t        (flow_dir / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(\"200 OK\\n\\n\" + sse)\n  711\t\n  712\t        # Write timing\n  713\t        timing = {\"request_start\": 1000.0, \"response_end\": 1002.5}\n  714\t        (flow_dir / \"timing.json\").write_text(json.dumps(timing))\n  715\t\n  716\t        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n  717\t\n  718\t        usage = json.loads((flow_dir / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n  719\t        assert usage[\"input_tokens\"] == 100\n  720\t        assert usage[\"output_tokens\"] == 50\n  721\t        assert \"extra_field\" not in usage\n  722\t        assert usage[\"timing\"][\"duration_ms\"] == 2500\n  723\t        assert not (flow_dir / \"timing.json\").exists()\n  724\t\n  725\t    def test_non_streaming_usage(self, tmp_path):\n  726\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  727\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  728\t\n  729\t        msg = {\"type\": \"message\", \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 200, \"output_tokens\": 100}}\n  730\t        (flow_dir / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(\"200 OK\\n\\n\" + json.dumps(msg))\n  731\t\n  732\t        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n  733\t\n  734\t        usage = json.loads((flow_dir / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n  735\t        assert usage[\"input_tokens\"] == 200\n  736\t\n  737\t    def test_no_usage_warns(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n  738\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  739\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  740\t        (flow_dir / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(\"200 OK\\n\\nno usage here\")\n  741\t\n  742\t        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n  743\t        assert not (flow_dir / \"usage.json\").exists()\n  744\t        assert \"Warning\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n  745\t\n  746\t    def test_timing_partial(self, tmp_path):\n  747\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  748\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  749\t\n  750\t        sse = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"output_tokens\":5}}\\n'\n  751\t        (flow_dir / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(sse)\n  752\t        (flow_dir / \"timing.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"request_start\": 1000.0}))\n  753\t\n  754\t        ef.extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n  755\t        usage = json.loads((flow_dir / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n  756\t        assert \"timing\" in usage\n  757\t        assert \"duration_ms\" not in usage[\"timing\"]\n  758\t\n  759\t\n  760\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  761\t# extract_prompts\n  762\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  763\tclass TestExtractPrompts:\n  764\t    def test_extracts_system_and_user(self, tmp_path):\n  765\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  766\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  767\t\n  768\t        body = {\n  769\t            \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"You are helpful.\"}],\n  770\t            \"messages\": [\n  771\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hello!\"}]},\n  772\t            ],\n  773\t        }\n  774\t        (flow_dir / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n  775\t\n  776\t        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n  777\t\n  778\t        assert (flow_dir / \"system_prompt.md\").read_text() == \"You are helpful.\"\n  779\t        assert (flow_dir / \"first_user_message.md\").read_text() == \"Hello!\"\n  780\t\n  781\t    def test_no_system(self, tmp_path):\n  782\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  783\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  784\t\n  785\t        body = {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hi\"}]}]}\n  786\t        (flow_dir / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n  787\t\n  788\t        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n  789\t        assert not (flow_dir / \"system_prompt.md\").exists()\n  790\t        assert (flow_dir / \"first_user_message.md\").read_text() == \"Hi\"\n  791\t\n  792\t    def test_invalid_json(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n  793\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  794\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  795\t        (flow_dir / \"request.json\").write_text(\"bad json\")\n  796\t\n  797\t        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n  798\t        assert \"Warning\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n  799\t\n  800\t    def test_string_content_user_message(self, tmp_path):\n  801\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  802\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  803\t\n  804\t        body = {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"plain string\"}]}\n  805\t        (flow_dir / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n  806\t\n  807\t        ef.extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n  808\t        # String content is not a list, so no first_user_message.md\n  809\t        assert not (flow_dir / \"first_user_message.md\").exists()\n  810\t\n  811\t\n  812\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  813\t# calculate_costs\n  814\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  815\tclass TestCalculateCosts:\n  816\t    def test_calculates_costs(self, tmp_path):\n  817\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  818\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  819\t\n  820\t        body = {\"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\"}\n  821\t        (flow_dir / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n  822\t\n  823\t        usage = {\n  824\t            \"input_tokens\": 1000,\n  825\t            \"output_tokens\": 500,\n  826\t            \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 200,\n  827\t            \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 100,\n  828\t        }\n  829\t        (flow_dir / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps(usage))\n  830\t\n  831\t        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n  832\t\n  833\t        result = json.loads((flow_dir / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n  834\t        assert \"cost\" in result\n  835\t        assert \"total\" in result[\"cost\"]\n  836\t        assert result[\"cost\"][\"total\"][\"dollars\"] \u003e 0\n  837\t        # Top-level token keys removed\n  838\t        assert \"input_tokens\" not in result\n  839\t        assert result[\"model\"] == \"claude-sonnet-4\"\n  840\t\n  841\t    def test_unknown_model_warns(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n  842\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  843\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  844\t\n  845\t        body = {\"model\": \"unknown-model-xyz\"}\n  846\t        (flow_dir / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n  847\t        (flow_dir / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"input_tokens\": 10}))\n  848\t\n  849\t        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n  850\t        assert \"Warning\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n  851\t\n  852\t    def test_no_model(self, tmp_path):\n  853\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  854\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  855\t\n  856\t        body = {\"messages\": []}\n  857\t        (flow_dir / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n  858\t        (flow_dir / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"input_tokens\": 10}))\n  859\t\n  860\t        ef.calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n  861\t        # usage.json should be unchanged\n  862\t        result = json.loads((flow_dir / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n  863\t        assert \"cost\" not in result\n  864\t\n  865\t\n  866\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  867\t# extract_file_ops\n  868\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  869\tclass TestExtractFileOps:\n  870\t    def test_reads_and_writes(self, tmp_path):\n  871\t        # Response with a Write tool_use\n  872\t        msg = {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": [\n  873\t            {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Write\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/tmp/out.py\", \"content\": \"hello\"}},\n  874\t        ]}\n  875\t        resp_path = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  876\t        resp_path.write_text(json.dumps(msg))\n  877\t\n  878\t        body = {\n  879\t            \"messages\": [\n  880\t                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [\n  881\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"r1\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/tmp/in.py\"}},\n  882\t                ]},\n  883\t                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [\n  884\t                    {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"r1\", \"content\": \"file content here\"},\n  885\t                ]},\n  886\t            ]\n  887\t        }\n  888\t\n  889\t        with patch(\"os.path.getsize\", return_value=100):\n  890\t            result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, str(resp_path))\n  891\t\n  892\t        assert result[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] == 1\n  893\t        assert result[\"input\"][\"total_read_chars\"] == len(\"file content here\")\n  894\t        assert result[\"output\"][\"unique_files_written\"] == 1\n  895\t\n  896\t    def test_no_ops(self, tmp_path):\n  897\t        resp_path = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n  898\t        resp_path.write_text(\"200 OK\\n\\nplain text\")\n  899\t\n  900\t        body = {\"messages\": []}\n  901\t        result = ef.extract_file_ops(body, str(resp_path))\n  902\t        assert result[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] == 0\n  903\t        assert result[\"output\"][\"files_written\"] == 0\n  904\t\n  905\t\n  906\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  907\t# export_parsed_responses\n  908\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  909\tclass TestExportParsedResponses:\n  910\t    def test_walks_and_exports(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n  911\t        flow_dir = tmp_path / \"a\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n  912\t        flow_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n  913\t\n  914\t        lines = [\n  915\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\"}}',\n  916\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"Hi\"}}',\n  917\t            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}',\n  918\t        ]\n  919\t        (flow_dir / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n  920\t\n  921\t        ef.export_parsed_responses(str(tmp_path))\n  922\t        assert (flow_dir / \"response_parsed.txt\").exists()\n  923\t\n  924\t\n  925\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  926\t# redact_flow_files (mock mitmproxy)\n  927\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  928\tclass TestRedactFlowFiles:\n  929\t    @patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\")\n  930\t    def test_no_flow_files(self, mock_glob):\n  931\t        mock_glob.return_value = []\n  932\t        ef.redact_flow_files(\"/some/dir\")  # Should not raise\n  933\t\n  934\t    @patch(\"export_flows.FlowWriter\")\n  935\t    @patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\")\n  936\t    @patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\")\n  937\t    def test_redacts_api_key(self, mock_glob, mock_reader_cls, mock_writer_cls, tmp_path):\n  938\t        from mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n  939\t\n  940\t        flow_path = str(tmp_path / \"test.flow\")\n  941\t        mock_glob.return_value = [flow_path]\n  942\t\n  943\t        # Create a mock that passes isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow)\n  944\t        mock_flow = MagicMock(spec=HTTPFlow)\n  945\t        # spec restricts attrs, so set them explicitly\n  946\t        mock_flow.request = MagicMock()\n  947\t        mock_flow.request.headers = MagicMock()\n  948\t        mock_flow.request.headers.get = MagicMock(\n  949\t            side_effect=lambda h: \"secret\" if h == b\"x-api-key\" else None\n  950\t        )\n  951\t\n  952\t        mock_reader = MagicMock()\n  953\t        mock_reader.stream.return_value = [mock_flow]\n  954\t        mock_reader_cls.return_value = mock_reader\n  955\t\n  956\t        # Create the file so open() works\n  957\t        with open(flow_path, \"wb\") as f:\n  958\t            f.write(b\"dummy\")\n  959\t\n  960\t        ef.redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n  961\t\n  962\t        # Should have written back\n  963\t        mock_writer_cls.assert_called_once()\n  964\t\n  965\t\n  966\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  967\t# export_flows (mock mitmproxy)\n  968\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  969\tclass TestExportFlows:\n  970\t    @patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\")\n  971\t    def test_no_flow_files(self, mock_glob, capsys):\n  972\t        mock_glob.return_value = []\n  973\t        ef.export_flows(\"/in\", \"/out\")\n  974\t        assert \"No *.flow files\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n  975\t\n  976\t    @patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\")\n  977\t    @patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\")\n  978\t    def test_exports_flows(self, mock_glob, mock_reader_cls, tmp_path, capsys):\n  979\t        from mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n  980\t\n  981\t        flow_path = str(tmp_path / \"vix.flow\")\n  982\t        mock_glob.return_value = [flow_path]\n  983\t\n  984\t        # Create mock flow that passes isinstance check\n  985\t        mock_flow = MagicMock(spec=HTTPFlow)\n  986\t        mock_flow.request = MagicMock()\n  987\t        mock_flow.response = MagicMock()\n  988\t        mock_flow.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\"\n  989\t        mock_flow.request.method = \"POST\"\n  990\t        mock_flow.request.headers.fields = []\n  991\t        mock_flow.request.get_text.return_value = '{\"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\", \"system\": [{\"text\": \"hi\"}], \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hello\"}]}'\n  992\t        mock_flow.request.timestamp_start = 1000.0\n  993\t        mock_flow.response.status_code = 200\n  994\t        mock_flow.response.reason = \"OK\"\n  995\t        mock_flow.response.headers.fields = []\n  996\t        mock_flow.response.get_text.return_value = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"}}\\n'\n  997\t        mock_flow.response.timestamp_end = 1002.0\n  998\t\n  999\t        mock_reader = MagicMock()\n 1000\t        mock_reader.stream.return_value = [mock_flow]\n 1001\t        mock_reader_cls.return_value = mock_reader\n 1002\t\n 1003\t        # Need to create a real file for open()\n 1004\t        with open(flow_path, \"wb\") as f:\n 1005\t            f.write(b\"dummy\")\n 1006\t\n 1007\t        out_dir = str(tmp_path / \"out\")\n 1008\t        os.makedirs(out_dir)\n 1009\t\n 1010\t        ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), out_dir)\n 1011\t\n 1012\t        output = capsys.readouterr().out\n 1013\t        assert \"Exported\" in output\n 1014\t\n 1015\t    @patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\")\n 1016\t    @patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\")\n 1017\t    def test_skips_count_token_and_quota(self, mock_glob, mock_reader_cls, tmp_path, capsys):\n 1018\t        from mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n 1019\t\n 1020\t        flow_path = str(tmp_path / \"vix.flow\")\n 1021\t        mock_glob.return_value = [flow_path]\n 1022\t\n 1023\t        # count_token flow\n 1024\t        flow1 = MagicMock(spec=HTTPFlow)\n 1025\t        flow1.request = MagicMock()\n 1026\t        flow1.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/count_tokens\"\n 1027\t        flow1.request.get_text.return_value = \"\"\n 1028\t\n 1029\t        # quota flow\n 1030\t        flow2 = MagicMock(spec=HTTPFlow)\n 1031\t        flow2.request = MagicMock()\n 1032\t        flow2.request.pretty_url = \"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\"\n 1033\t        flow2.request.method = \"POST\"\n 1034\t        flow2.request.get_text.return_value = json.dumps({\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"quota\"}]})\n 1035\t\n 1036\t        mock_reader = MagicMock()\n 1037\t        mock_reader.stream.return_value = [flow1, flow2]\n 1038\t        mock_reader_cls.return_value = mock_reader\n 1039\t\n 1040\t        with open(flow_path, \"wb\") as f:\n 1041\t            f.write(b\"dummy\")\n 1042\t\n 1043\t        out_dir = str(tmp_path / \"out\")\n 1044\t        os.makedirs(out_dir)\n 1045\t\n 1046\t        ef.export_flows(str(tmp_path), out_dir)\n 1047\t        output = capsys.readouterr().out\n 1048\t        assert \"Exported 0 flows\" in output\n 1049\t\n 1050\t\n 1051\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 1052\t# summarize_usage\n 1053\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 1054\tclass TestSummarizeUsage:\n 1055\t    def test_summarizes(self, tmp_path):\n 1056\t        agent_dir = tmp_path / \"vix\"\n 1057\t        step_dir = agent_dir / \"1\" / \"1\"\n 1058\t        step_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n 1059\t\n 1060\t        usage = {\n 1061\t            \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\",\n 1062\t            \"cost\": {\n 1063\t                \"input\": {\"tokens\": 100, \"dollars\": 0.001},\n 1064\t                \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": 50, \"dollars\": 0.0005},\n 1065\t                \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": 20, \"dollars\": 0.0001},\n 1066\t                \"output\": {\"tokens\": 30, \"dollars\": 0.003},\n 1067\t                \"total\": {\"tokens\": 200, \"dollars\": 0.0046},\n 1068\t            },\n 1069\t            \"timing\": {\"request_start\": 1000.0, \"response_end\": 1002.0, \"duration_ms\": 2000},\n 1070\t        }\n 1071\t        (step_dir / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps(usage))\n 1072\t\n 1073\t        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n 1074\t\n 1075\t        summary = json.loads((agent_dir / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n 1076\t        assert summary[\"title\"] == \"vix\"\n 1077\t        assert summary[\"total\"][\"request_count\"] == 1\n 1078\t        assert summary[\"color\"] == \"#7B2FBE\"\n 1079\t\n 1080\t    def test_skips_non_agent_dirs(self, tmp_path):\n 1081\t        # Create a file, not a dir\n 1082\t        (tmp_path / \"readme.txt\").write_text(\"hi\")\n 1083\t        # Create dir without numbered subdirs\n 1084\t        (tmp_path / \"other\").mkdir()\n 1085\t        (tmp_path / \"other\" / \"notes.txt\").write_text(\"hi\")\n 1086\t\n 1087\t        ef.summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n 1088\t        # No crash, no summary files\n 1089\t        assert not (tmp_path / \"other\" / \"usage.json\").exists()\n 1090\t","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me run the tests first to see the current state, then implement the refactoring step by step.","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01S9bc5pD6fLr4Nb8NkkCZFm","input":{"command":"cd /workspace \u0026\u0026 python -m pytest test_export_flows.py -q 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -20","reason":"Check current test state before starting refactoring","reason_to_use_instead_of_read_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_edit_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_glob_files_tool":"N/A"},"name":"bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S9bc5pD6fLr4Nb8NkkCZFm","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"bash: line 1: python: command not found\n","type":"text"}],"type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"id":"toolu_01JVngLpe8GDrixhD9kp8SJU","input":{"command":"cd /workspace \u0026\u0026 python3 -m pytest test_export_flows.py -q 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -20","reason":"Check current test state be